    "t(Vec::count(&none, [](ref<i32, shared> x) : bool { *x > 5 }) == 0);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}slice_eq\u{1f}fn\u{1f}"
    "export fn slice_eq<T: eq>(slice<T, shared> a, slice<T, shared> b) : bool\u{1f}Whether `a` and `b` have th"
    "e same length and equal elements in the same order.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn slice_eq<T: eq>(slice<T, shared> a, s"
    "lice<T, shared> b) : bool\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    Whether `a` and `b` have the same length an"
    "d equal elements in the same order.\n\n    Elements are compared with `==` in index order, stopping at"
    " the first difference. Slices have no `==`\n    of their own; a `Vec` is passed as `&v[0..$]`, an arr"
    "ay as `&a[0..$]`.\n\n    Example, \"slice_eq: Vec and array\":\n        Vec<u8> v = Vec::new();\n        V"
    "ec::push(&mut v, 1);\n        Vec::push(&mut v, 2);\n        array<u8, 2> a = [1, 2];\n        assert(s"
    "lice_eq(&v, &a));\n        assert(!slice_eq(&v[0..1], &a));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::collections\u{1f}Vec::index_of\u{1f}fn\u{1f}expor"
    "t fn Vec::index_of<T: eq>(ref<Vec<T>, shared> v, probe<T> x) : Option<usize>\u{1f}The index of the first "
