    "_remove<K, V>(ref<HashMap<K, V>, exclusive> m, probe<K> k) : Option<V>\u{1f}Removes `k` and returns its v"
    "alue, in constant time; `None` when `k` is absent.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HashMap::swap_remove<K, V>(ref<HashMap"
    "<K, V>, exclusive> m, probe<K> k) : Option<V>\n    in `std::collections`\n\n    Removes `k` and returns"
    " its value, in constant time; `None` when `k` is absent.\n\n    The last entry moves into the removed "
    "one's place, so the insertion order is not kept;\n    `HashMap::remove` keeps it. The removed key is "
