    " new, empty priority queue in the order `less` gives: the element no other goes before comes out\n   "
    " first.\n\n    `less` is true when its first argument goes before its second and must be a strict weak"
    " order, as for\n    `Vec::sort_by`. A largest-first queue passes a `less` that answers \"greater\".\n\n  "
    "  Example, \"PriorityQueue::new_by: first in, first out among equals\":\n        auto larger_tens = []("
    "ref<i32, shared> a, ref<i32, shared> b) : bool { *a / 10 > *b / 10 };\n        PriorityQueue<i32> q ="
    " PriorityQueue::new_by(larger_tens);\n        PriorityQueue::push(&mut q, 15);\n        PriorityQueue:"
