    " last occurrence\":\n        assert(StringView::rfind(\"abcabc\", \"bc\") == Some(4: usize));\n        asse"
    "rt(StringView::rfind(\"abc\", \"d\") == None);\n        assert(StringView::rfind(\"abc\", \"\") == Some(3: us"
    "ize));\n        assert(StringView::rfind(\"\", \"\") == Some(0: usize));\n\n    Example, \"StringView::find:"
    " positions and the empty text\":\n        assert(StringView::contains(\"abc\", \"\"));\n        assert(Stri"
    "ngView::find(\"abcabc\", \"c\") == Some(2: usize));\n        assert(StringView::find(\"abc\", \"d\") == None)"
    ";\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::starts_with\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::starts_with(StringView v, StringView "
    "t) : bool\u{1f}Whether `v` begins with `t`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::starts_with(StringView v, StringView t"
    ") : bool\n    in `std::text`\n\n    Whether `v` begins with `t`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::ends_with\u{1f}fn\u{1f}e"
    "xport fn StringView::ends_with(StringView v, StringView t) : bool\u{1f}Whether `v` ends with `t`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export"
    " fn StringView::ends_with(StringView v, StringView t) : bool\n    in `std::text`\n\n    Whether `v` end"
    "s with `t`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::contains\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::contains(StringView v, StringV"
    "iew t) : bool\u{1f}Whether `t` occurs in `v`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::contains(StringView v, StringView t)"
    " : bool\n    in `std::text`\n\n    Whether `t` occurs in `v`.\n\n    The empty text is in every text.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}s"
    "td::text\u{1f}StringView::trim_start\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::trim_start(StringView v) : StringView\u{1f}The v"
    "iew `v` without the ASCII white space at its start.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::trim_start(StringView v) "
    ": StringView\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The view `v` without the ASCII white space at its start.\n\n    W"
    "hite space is what `ascii_is_space` accepts.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::trim_end\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringVie"
    "w::trim_end(StringView v) : StringView\u{1f}The view `v` without the ASCII white space at its end.\u{1f}\u{1f}expor"
    "t fn StringView::trim_end(StringView v) : StringView\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The view `v` without th"
    "e ASCII white space at its end.\n\n    White space is what `ascii_is_space` accepts.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}Strin"
    "gView::trim\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::trim(StringView v) : StringView\u{1f}The view `v` without the ASCII "
    "white space at either end.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::trim(StringView v) : StringView\n    in `std::text`"
    "\n\n    The view `v` without the ASCII white space at either end.\n\n    White space is what `ascii_is_s"
    "pace` accepts; there is no Unicode white space.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::split\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringVie"
    "w::split(StringView v, StringView sep) : Vec<StringView> from v\u{1f}The parts of `v` between occurrences"
    " of `sep`, in order, each a view of the same text.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::split(StringView v, String"
    "View sep) : Vec<StringView> from v\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The parts of `v` between occurrences of `"
    "sep`, in order, each a view of the same text.\n\n    Empty parts are kept: `\"a,,b\"` gives three parts,"
    " and empty text one empty part. An empty `sep` gives `v`\n    whole. The parts are views of `v` alone"
    " (`from v`), so `sep` is any text. `StringView::split_whitespace`\n    gives words without empty part"
    "s.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::split: empty fields\":\n        StringView line = \"a,,b\";\n        Vec<St"
    "ringView> parts = StringView::split(line, \",\");\n        assert(Vec::len(&parts) == 3);\n        asser"
    "t(parts[1] == \"\");\n        assert(parts[2] == \"b\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::char_count\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn "
    "StringView::char_count(StringView v) : usize\u{1f}The number of characters (code points) in `v`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export "
    "fn StringView::char_count(StringView v) : usize\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The number of characters (co"
    "de points) in `v`.\n\n    `StringView::len` counts bytes; a character is one to four bytes. A characte"
    "r is a Unicode scalar value,\n    so `\"e\\u{301}\"` is two. Nothing is allocated.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringVie"
    "w::chars\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::chars(StringView v) : Vec<StringView>\u{1f}The characters of `v`, in or"
    "der, each a view of that character's one to four bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::chars(StringView v) :"
    " Vec<StringView>\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The characters of `v`, in order, each a view of that charac"
    "ter's one to four bytes.\n\n    Empty text gives an empty `Vec`. The `Vec` is new (one allocation); th"
    "e views borrow what `v` borrows.\n    `StringView::code_point` reads a character's code point, and `S"
    "tringView::char_count` counts without the\n    `Vec`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::replace\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn St"
    "ringView::replace(StringView v, StringView from, StringView to) : String\u{1f}A new `String` holding `v` "
    "with every occurrence of `from` replaced by `to`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::replace(StringView v, Strin"
    "gView from, StringView to) : String\n    in `std::text`\n\n    A new `String` holding `v` with every oc"
    "currence of `from` replaced by `to`.\n\n    Occurrences are found left to right and do not overlap; an"
    " empty `from` occurs nowhere, so the result is\n    then a copy of `v`.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::re"
    "place: no overlaps\":\n        String r = StringView::replace(\"aaa\", \"aa\", \"b\");\n        assert(r == \""
    "ba\");\n        String same = StringView::replace(\"abc\", \"\", \"x\");\n        assert(same == \"abc\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}st"
    "d::text\u{1f}StringView::join\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::join(slice<StringView, shared> parts, StringView s"
    "ep) : String\u{1f}The texts of `parts`, in order, with `sep` between each two, in a new `String`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export"
    " fn StringView::join(slice<StringView, shared> parts, StringView sep) : String\n    in `std::text`\n\n "
    "   The texts of `parts`, in order, with `sep` between each two, in a new `String`.\n\n    No parts giv"
    "e an empty `String`. `String::join` joins a slice of `String`s.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::join: sep"
    "arators between\":\n        Vec<StringView> parts = Vec::new();\n        Vec::push(&mut parts, StringVi"
    "ew::of(\"a\"));\n        Vec::push(&mut parts, StringView::of(\"b\"));\n        Vec::push(&mut parts, Stri"
    "ngView::of(\"c\"));\n        String j = StringView::join(&parts, \", \");\n        assert(j == \"a, b, c\");"
    "\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::join\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::join(slice<String, shared> parts, StringView sep) : S"
    "tring\u{1f}The texts of the `String`s in `parts`, in order, with `sep` between each two, in a new `String"
    "`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn String::join(slice<String, shared> parts, StringView sep) : String\n    in `std::text`\n"
    "\n    The texts of the `String`s in `parts`, in order, with `sep` between each two, in a new `String`"
    ".\n\n    No parts give an empty `String`. `StringView::join` joins a slice of views.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}Strin"
    "g::copy\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::copy(StringView v) : String\u{1f}A new `String` holding a copy of the text o"
    "f `v`: a view, a `str`, a literal, or `&s` of a `String`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn String::copy(StringView v) : St"
    "ring\n    in `std::text`\n\n    A new `String` holding a copy of the text of `v`: a view, a `str`, a li"
    "teral, or `&s` of a `String`.\n\n    `String::clone(&s)` copies a whole `String` the same way.\n\n    Ex"
    "ample, \"StringView::chars: bytes and characters\":\n        String s = \"h\\u{e9}!\";\n        assert(Stri"
    "ngView::len(&s) == 4);\n        assert(StringView::char_count(&s) == 3);\n        Vec<StringView> cs ="
    " StringView::chars(&s);\n        assert(StringView::len(cs[1]) == 2);\n        assert(StringView::code"
    "_point(cs[1]) == Some(0xe9: u32));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::strip_prefix\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::str"
    "ip_prefix(StringView v, StringView t) : Option<StringView> from v\u{1f}The rest of `v` after `t` when `v`"
    " begins with `t`, else `None`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::strip_prefix(StringView v, StringView t) : Opt"
    "ion<StringView> from v\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The rest of `v` after `t` when `v` begins with `t`, e"
    "lse `None`.\n\n    It reads an option's value: `StringView::strip_prefix(a, \"--name=\")` gives the valu"
    "e, or `None` for\n    another argument.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::strip_prefix: an option's value\":\n"
    "        StringView a = \"--name=value\";\n        assert(Option::unwrap(StringView::strip_prefix(a, \"--"
    "name=\")) == \"value\");\n        assert(Option::is_none(&StringView::strip_prefix(a, \"--other=\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}s"
    "td::text\u{1f}StringView::strip_suffix\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::strip_suffix(StringView v, StringView t) "
    ": Option<StringView> from v\u{1f}The part of `v` before `t` when `v` ends with `t`, else `None`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export "
    "fn StringView::strip_suffix(StringView v, StringView t) : Option<StringView> from v\n    in `std::tex"
    "t`\n\n    The part of `v` before `t` when `v` ends with `t`, else `None`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::line"
    "s\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::lines(StringView v) : Vec<StringView>\u{1f}The lines of `v`: the parts between"
    " `\\n` bytes, each without a `\\r` just before its `\\n`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::lines(StringView v) : "
    "Vec<StringView>\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The lines of `v`: the parts between `\\n` bytes, each without"
    " a `\\r` just before its `\\n`.\n\n    There is no empty line after a final `\\n`, so `\"a\\nb\\n\"` and `\"a\\"
    "nb\"` both give `a` and `b`; `\"\\n\\n\"`\n    gives two empty lines, and empty text none. A `\\r` not foll"
    "owed by `\\n` stays in its line.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::lines: line endings\":\n        StringView "
    "text = \"one\\r\\ntwo\\n\\nthree\\n\";\n        Vec<StringView> ls = StringView::lines(text);\n        assert"
    "(Vec::len(&ls) == 4);\n        assert(ls[0] == \"one\");\n        assert(ls[2] == \"\");\n        assert(ls"
    "[3] == \"three\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::split_whitespace\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::split_whitespace("
    "StringView v) : Vec<StringView>\u{1f}The words of `v`: the runs of bytes that are not ASCII white space, "
    "in order.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::split_whitespace(StringView v) : Vec<StringView>\n    in `std::text`"
    "\n\n    The words of `v`: the runs of bytes that are not ASCII white space, in order.\n\n    No word is "
    "empty, so leading, trailing and repeated white space make no difference. White space is what\n    `as"
    "cii_is_space` accepts.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::split_whitespace: runs of spaces\":\n        Vec<Str"
    "ingView> w = StringView::split_whitespace(\"  to  be\\tor \");\n        assert(Vec::len(&w) == 3);\n     "
    "   assert(w[0] == \"to\");\n        assert(w[2] == \"or\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::code_point\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export "
    "fn StringView::code_point(StringView v) : Option<u32>\u{1f}The code point of the first character of `v`, "
    "or `None` when `v` is empty.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::code_point(StringView v) : Option<u32>\n    in `s"
    "td::text`\n\n    The code point of the first character of `v`, or `None` when `v` is empty.\n\n    With "
    "`StringView::chars`, it reads every character of a text in turn.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::push_code_point"
    "\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::push_code_point(ref<String, exclusive> s, u32 cp)\u{1f}Appends the character with c"
    "ode point `cp` to `s`, as one to four UTF-8 bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn String::push_code_point(ref<String, ex"
    "clusive> s, u32 cp)\n    in `std::text`\n\n    Appends the character with code point `cp` to `s`, as on"
    "e to four UTF-8 bytes.\n\n    A value that is no character (a surrogate, `0xD800` to `0xDFFF`, or abov"
    "e `0x10FFFF`) appends U+FFFD, the\n    replacement character, so `s` stays UTF-8.\n\n    Example, \"Stri"
    "ng::push_code_point: a surrogate\":\n        String s = String::new();\n        String::push_code_point"
    "(&mut s, 0x41);\n        String::push_code_point(&mut s, 0xD800);\n        assert(s == \"A\\u{fffd}\");\n\n"
    "    Example, \"StringView::lines: a foreach takes the parts as it goes\":\n        StringView text = \"o"
    "ne\\r\\ntwo\\n\\nthree\\n\";\n        Vec<StringView> ls = StringView::lines(text);\n        usize n = 0;\n  "
    "      foreach (i, l in StringView::lines(text))\n        {\n            assert(l == ls[i]);\n          "
    "  n += 1;\n        }\n        assert(n == 4);\n        n = 0;\n        foreach (w in StringView::split_w"
    "hitespace(\"  to  be\\tor \"))\n        {\n            n += StringView::len(w);\n        }\n        assert("
    "n == 6);\n        n = 0;\n        foreach (f in StringView::split(\"a,,b\", \",\"))\n        {\n            "
    "n += 1;\n        }\n        assert(n == 3);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn StringView::par"
    "se<T>(StringView v) : Result<T, ParseError>\u{1f}The number the text of `v` holds, as a `T`: an integer t"
    "ype, `f32` or `f64`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::parse<T>(StringView v) : Result<T, ParseError>\n    in `s"
    "td::text`\n\n    The number the text of `v` holds, as a `T`: an integer type, `f32` or `f64`.\n\n    Par"
    "sed in place, by the rules and with the errors of `[Parse]` (spec/21 §2d): the whole text or nothin"
    "g, so white\n    space around the number must be trimmed first.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}StringView::parse_radix\u{1f}f"
    "n\u{1f}export fn StringView::parse_radix<T: integer>(StringView v, u32 radix) : Result<T, ParseError>\u{1f}The"
    " integer the text of `v` writes in base `radix` (2 to 36), as a `T`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn StringView::parse_ra"
    "dix<T: integer>(StringView v, u32 radix) : Result<T, ParseError>\n    in `std::text`\n    requires\n   "
    "     radix >= 2 && radix <= 36, assert_failed, \"StringView::parse_radix: the radix is from 2 to 36, "
    "not %v\", radix\n\n    The integer the text of `v` writes in base `radix` (2 to 36), as a `T`.\n\n    Dig"
    "its are `0`-`9` then `a`-`z` or `A`-`Z`, with no prefix such as `0x`; a leading `-` for a signed `T`"
    ".\n    The whole text or nothing, as `StringView::parse`: `Err(Empty)`, `Err(Invalid(position))` for "
    "a character\n    that is no digit of the base, `Err(OutOfRange)` when the number does not fit. A radi"
    "x outside 2 to 36 is\n    a fault.\n\n    Example, \"StringView::parse_radix: bases, signs and errors\":\n"
    "        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u8>(\"ff\", 16) == Ok(255));\n        assert(StringView::parse_r"
    "adix<u8>(\"FF\", 16) == Ok(255));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u8>(\"100\", 16) == Err(OutOfRa"
    "nge));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<i8>(\"-80\", 16) == Ok(-128));\n        assert(StringView"
    "::parse_radix<i8>(\"80\", 16) == Err(OutOfRange));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u32>(\"777\", "
    "8) == Ok(511));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u64>(\"1010\", 2) == Ok(10));\n        assert(St"
    "ringView::parse_radix<u32>(\"zz\", 36) == Ok(1295));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u32>(\"12g\""
    ", 16) == Err(Invalid(2)));\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<u32>(\"-1\", 16) == Err(Invalid(0)))"
    ";\n        assert(StringView::parse_radix<i32>(\"-\", 10) == Err(Invalid(1)));\n        assert(StringVie"
    "w::parse_radix<u32>(\"\", 10) == Err(Empty));\n\n    Example, \"StringView::parse: no white space\":\n     "
    "   StringView v = \" 42 \";\n        assert(StringView::parse<u32>(v) == Err(Invalid(0)));\n        asse"
    "rt(StringView::parse<u32>(StringView::trim(v)) == Ok(42));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::append\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn S"
    "tring::append<T>(ref<String, exclusive> s, T x)\u{1f}Appends `x` to `s` as text: the bytes `printf(\"%v\", "
    "x)` would write.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn String::append<T>(ref<String, exclusive> s, T x)\n    in `std::text`\n\n   "
    " Appends `x` to `s` as text: the bytes `printf(\"%v\", x)` would write.\n\n    `x` is a `str`, a `String"
    "View`, a `ref<String, shared>`, an integer, `f32`, `f64` or `bool`; another type\n    is rejected at "
    "the call. A float is written in the shortest digits that read back as the same value\n    (`1.0`, `0."
    "1`). `String::appendf` appends formatted text.\n\n    Example, \"String::append: numbers as printf writ"
    "es them\":\n        String s = \"x = \";\n        String::append(&mut s, 1.0);\n        String::append(&mu"
    "t s, \", n = \");\n        String::append(&mut s, 42: u8);\n        assert(s == \"x = 1.0, n = 42\");\n\n   "
    " Example, \"StringView::parse: the three errors\":\n        String a = \"12x4\";\n        assert(StringVie"
    "w::parse<i32>(&a) == Err(Invalid(2)));\n        String b = \"300\";\n        assert(StringView::parse<u8"
    ">(&b) == Err(OutOfRange));\n        String c = \"\";\n        assert(StringView::parse<i32>(&c) == Err(E"
    "mpty));\n        String d = \"-17\";\n        assert(StringView::parse<i32>(&d) == Ok(-17));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text"
    "\u{1f}String::from_view\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::from_view\u{1f}\u{1f}removed\u{1f}export fn String::from_view\n    in `std::"
    "text`\n    removed: write String::copy(…): a copy of a view's text (D-0312)\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::to_"
    "ascii_lower\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn String::to_ascii_lower\u{1f}\u{1f}removed\u{1f}export fn String::to_ascii_lower\n    in `st"
    "d::text`\n    removed: write StringView::to_ascii_lower(&s): it takes the text's view (D-0312)\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std:"
