    "ish one before any starts the next.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Barrier::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Barrier::new(usize parties"
    ") : Barrier\u{1f}A barrier for `parties` threads.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Barrier::new(usize parties) : Barrier\n    in"
    " `std::sync`\n    requires\n        parties != 0, barrier_zero_parties\n\n    A barrier for `parties` th"
    "reads.\n\n    Faults (`barrier_zero_parties`) when `parties` is 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Barrier::wait\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export"
    " fn Barrier::wait(ref<Barrier, shared> b) : bool\u{1f}Waits until `parties` threads have called it, then "
    "lets them all go on.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Barrier::wait(ref<Barrier, shared> b) : bool\n    in `std::sync`\n\n   "
    " Waits until `parties` threads have called it, then lets them all go on.\n\n    `true` for the last th"
    "read to arrive, the one that released the others, and `false` for the rest, so one\n    thread of eac"
    "h round can do something once. A wait that fewer threads than `parties` can ever reach\n    faults (`"
    "deadlock`).\n\n    Example, \"Barrier::wait: rounds, one leader each\":\n        Barrier b = Barrier::new"
    "(4);\n        Atomic<u32> leaders = Atomic::new(0: u32);\n        Atomic<u32> seen = Atomic::new(0: u3"
    "2);\n        Vec<handle<void>> hs = Vec::new();\n        for (u32 i = 0; i < 4; i += 1)\n        {\n    "
    "        Vec::push(&mut hs, spawn(move [](\n                ref<Barrier, shared> b,\n                re"
    "f<Atomic<u32>, shared> leaders,\n                ref<Atomic<u32>, shared> seen,\n                u32 i"
    "d,\n            )\n            {\n                for (u32 round = 0; round < 3; round += 1)\n          "
    "      {\n                    _ = Atomic::fetch_add(seen, 1);\n                    if (Barrier::wait(b)"
    ")\n                    {\n                        _ = Atomic::fetch_add(leaders, 1);\n                 "
    "       assert(Atomic::load(seen) == 4 * (round + 1));   // everyone wrote before anyone read\n       "
    "             }\n                    _ = Barrier::wait(b);                                 // the read"
    " phase ends together too\n                }\n            }, &b, &leaders, &seen, i));\n        }\n      "
    "  foreach (h in hs)\n        {\n            join(h);\n        }\n        assert(Atomic::load(&leaders) ="
    "= 3 && Atomic::load(&seen) == 12);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Semaphore\u{1f}A count of p"
    "ermits that threads take and give back.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Semaphore\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    A count of "
    "permits that threads take and give back.\n\n    Shared by reference, as a `mutex` is. `acquire` takes "
    "one permit, waiting while there is none; `release`\n    gives one back, or adds one. It bounds how ma"
    "ny threads do something at once (connections open, workers\n    busy); made with 0 permits, it hands "
    "events from one thread to another, each `release` letting one\n    `acquire` through.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Sem"
    "aphore::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::new(usize permits) : Semaphore\u{1f}A semaphore with `permits` permit"
    "s; 0 is allowed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::new(usize permits) : Semaphore\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    A sema"
    "phore with `permits` permits; 0 is allowed.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::acquire\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::a"
    "cquire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s)\u{1f}Takes one permit, waiting while there is none.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore"
    "::acquire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s)\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Takes one permit, waiting while there is"
    " none.\n\n    Permits are not handed out in arrival order. A wait no thread can end faults (`deadlock`"
    ").\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::try_acquire\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::try_acquire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s) "
    ": bool\u{1f}Takes one permit if one is free, without waiting: `true` when it did.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::t"
    "ry_acquire(ref<Semaphore, shared> s) : bool\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Takes one permit if one is free,"
    " without waiting: `true` when it did.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::release\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::release"
    "(ref<Semaphore, shared> s)\u{1f}Gives one permit back, or adds one; a thread waiting in `acquire` wakes.\u{1f}"
    "\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::release(ref<Semaphore, shared> s)\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Gives one permit bac"
    "k, or adds one; a thread waiting in `acquire` wakes.\n\n    Faults (`arith_overflow`) when the permits"
    " would exceed what `usize` counts.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Semaphore::available\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::availabl"
    "e(ref<Semaphore, shared> s) : usize\u{1f}How many permits are free now: a snapshot another thread may cha"
    "nge at once.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Semaphore::available(ref<Semaphore, shared> s) : usize\n    in `std::sync`\n\n "
    "   How many permits are free now: a snapshot another thread may change at once.\n\n    Example, \"Semap"
    "hore: a bound and a hand-over\":\n        Semaphore limit = Semaphore::new(2);\n        Atomic<u32> act"
    "ive = Atomic::new(0: u32);\n        Atomic<u32> peak = Atomic::new(0: u32);\n        Vec<handle<void>>"
    " hs = Vec::new();\n        for (u32 i = 0; i < 6; i += 1)\n        {\n            Vec::push(&mut hs, sp"
    "awn(move [](\n                ref<Semaphore, shared> limit,\n                ref<Atomic<u32>, shared> "
    "active,\n                ref<Atomic<u32>, shared> peak,\n            )\n            {\n                S"
    "emaphore::acquire(limit);\n                _ = Atomic::fetch_max(peak, Atomic::fetch_add(active, 1) +"
    " 1);\n                _ = Atomic::fetch_sub(active, 1);\n                Semaphore::release(limit);\n  "
    "          }, &limit, &active, &peak));\n        }\n        foreach (h in hs)\n        {\n            joi"
    "n(h);\n        }\n        assert(Atomic::load(&peak) <= 2 && Semaphore::available(&limit) == 2);\n     "
    "   assert(Semaphore::try_acquire(&limit) && Semaphore::try_acquire(&limit) && !Semaphore::try_acquir"
    "e(&limit));\n\n        Semaphore events = Semaphore::new(0);\n        handle<u32> h = spawn(move [](ref"
    "<Semaphore, shared> e) : u32\n        {\n            Semaphore::acquire(e);\n            Semaphore::acq"
    "uire(e);\n            Semaphore::acquire(e);\n            3\n        }, &events);\n        Semaphore::re"
    "lease(&events);\n        Semaphore::release(&events);\n        Semaphore::release(&events);\n        as"
    "sert(join(h) == 3 && Semaphore::available(&events) == 0);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Once\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Once"
    "\u{1f}Something done once, by whichever thread gets there first.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Once\n    in `std::sync`\n\n"
    "    Something done once, by whichever thread gets there first.\n\n    Shared by reference, as a `mutex"
    "` is. `Once::call(&o, f)` runs `f` the first time any thread calls it;\n    every other call, on any "
    "thread, returns once that run has finished, without running `f`: initialising\n    what several threa"
    "ds share, lazily and exactly once. Should `f` fault, the `Once` is as before, and the\n    next calle"
    "r runs `f` afresh.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Once::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Once::new() : Once\u{1f}A `Once` whose `f` has not "
    "run.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Once::new() : Once\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    A `Once` whose `f` has not run.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sy"
    "nc\u{1f}Once::call\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Once::call(ref<Once, shared> o, fn() f)\u{1f}Runs `f` if no call has run it ye"
    "t; otherwise waits until the call that is running it has finished.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Once::call(ref<Once, s"
    "hared> o, fn() f)\n    in `std::sync`\n\n    Runs `f` if no call has run it yet; otherwise waits until "
    "the call that is running it has finished.\n\n    `f` runs on the calling thread. After `call` returns,"
    " on any thread, `f` has run to its end exactly once\n    (unless it faulted, and then the next caller"
    " runs it again).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::sync\u{1f}Once::is_done\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Once::is_done(ref<Once, shared> o) : bool\u{1f}Wh"
    "ether `f` has run to its end.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Once::is_done(ref<Once, shared> o) : bool\n    in `std::sync"
    "`\n\n    Whether `f` has run to its end.\n\n    Example, \"Once::call: once among four threads\":\n        "
    "Once o = Once::new();\n        Atomic<u32> runs = Atomic::new(0: u32);\n        Vec<handle<bool>> hs ="
