    ".\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn SocketAddr::parse(StringView text) : Result<SocketAddr, ParseError>\n    in `std::net`\n\n"
    "    Reads an address and a port written `a.b.c.d:port` or `[v6]:port`.\n\n    - `Err(Empty)` for \"\".\n "
    "   - `Err(Invalid(i))` at the first byte that does not fit; `i` is the address's first byte when the"
    "\n      address is not one (an IPv6 address must be in brackets, an IPv4 address must not).\n    - `Er"
    "r(OutOfRange)` for a port above 65535.\n\n    Example, \"SocketAddr::parse: IPv6 needs brackets\":\n     "
    "   SocketAddr a = Result::unwrap(SocketAddr::parse(\"[::1]:8080\"));\n        assert(a.port == 8080);\n "
    "       assert(SocketAddr::text(&a) == \"[::1]:8080\");\n        match (SocketAddr::parse(\"::1:8080\"))\n "
    "       {\n            Err(Invalid(i)) : assert(i == 0),\n            _               : assert(false),\n"
