    "tion: a stream of bytes each way.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct TcpStream\n    in `std::net`\n\n    A TCP con"
    "nection: a stream of bytes each way.\n\n    The bytes on the wire are exactly those written, in order,"
    " with no framing or encoding added, and a\n    `read` gives whatever part of them has arrived. Calls "
    "block until they complete or the stream's timeout\n    passes (`set_read_timeout_ms`, `set_write_time"
    "out_ms`). Dropping the stream closes it; the connection\n    closes when the last stream on it (`try_"
    "clone`) is dropped. Formatted text is sent with\n    `TcpStream::printf(s, format, …)`, as `File::p"
    "rintf` writes to a file.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpListener::bind\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TcpListener::bind(SocketAddr a) :"
