    "td::x509`\n\n    The DER element at `at` in `buf`, or `None` when it is not well-formed.\n\n    Well-for"
    "med means a single-byte tag, the shortest length form, at most four length bytes, no indefinite\n    "
    "length, and contents inside `buf`. Read an element's first child by calling it again at `start`, and"
    " the\n    element after it at `next`.\n\n    Example, \"der_read: an element, its child, and a long form"
    " refused\":\n        array<u8, 5> der = [0x30, 0x03, 0x02, 0x01, 0x05];\n        Der seq = Option::unwr"
    "ap(der_read(&der, 0));\n        assert(seq.tag == 0x30 && seq.start == 2 && seq.end == 5 && seq.next "
    "== 5);\n        Der int = Option::unwrap(der_read(&der, seq.start));\n        assert(int.tag == 0x02 &"
    "& der[int.start] == 5);\n        array<u8, 4> long_form = [0x04, 0x81, 0x01, 0x00];\n        assert(Op"
