    "256 or P-384 key.\n    - `Ed25519Key`: an Ed25519 key, 32 bytes.\n    - `UnsupportedKey`: a key of ano"
    "ther algorithm; a certificate with one parses, but no signature verifies\n      under it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509"
    "\u{1f}SignatureScheme\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum SignatureScheme\u{1f}A signature algorithm with its hash, as certificat"
    "es and TLS name them.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum SignatureScheme\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    A signature algorithm wit"
    "h its hash, as certificates and TLS name them.\n\n    - `RsaPkcs1(h)`: RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 over the hash"
    " `h`.\n    - `RsaPss(h)`: RSASSA-PSS over `h`, with MGF1 over `h` and a salt as long as its digest.\n "
    "   - `Ecdsa(h)`: ECDSA over `h`.\n    - `Ed25519`: Ed25519, over the message itself.\n    - `Unsupport"
    "edSignature`: another algorithm; nothing verifies or signs with it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}Certificate\u{1f}struct\u{1f}e"
    "xport struct Certificate\u{1f}A parsed X.509 certificate (RFC 5280), v3 or older.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Certific"
    "ate\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    A parsed X.509 certificate (RFC 5280), v3 or older.\n\n    - `der`: the wh"
    "ole certificate; `tbs`: the signed part; `signature`: the signature over `tbs`, made with\n      `sch"
    "eme`.\n    - `issuer`, `subject`: the names' DER, compared whole.\n    - `common_name`: the subject's "
    "last common name, empty when there is none; host matching does not consult\n      it.\n    - `not_befo"
    "re`, `not_after`: the validity.\n    - `dns_names`, `ip_addresses`: the subject alternative names' DN"
    "S names and IP addresses.\n    - `is_ca`, `max_path_len`: the basic constraints; `max_path_len` is -1"
    " when there is no limit.\n    - `can_sign_certificates`: key usage's keyCertSign, `true` when there i"
    "s no key usage.\n    - `server_auth`: extended key usage allows server authentication or any use, `tr"
    "ue` when there is no\n      extended key usage.\n    - `unhandled_critical`: a critical extension othe"
    "r than certificate policies or name constraints was not\n      understood, so the certificate is not "
    "usable.\n    - `key`: the subject's public key.\n\n    Not independently audited: `std::x509` is implem"
    "ented to the standards its documentation names, tested\n    against OpenSSL, and fuzzed continuously,"
    " but it has not been independently audited.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}Certificate::parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Certificate:"
    ":parse(slice<u8, shared> der) : Result<Certificate, CertError>\u{1f}The certificate whose DER is `der` (R"
    "FC 5280 §4.1), or `Err(BadEncoding)`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Certificate::parse(slice<u8, shared> der) : Result"
    "<Certificate, CertError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The certificate whose DER is `der` (RFC 5280 §4.1)"
    ", or `Err(BadEncoding)`.\n\n    `der` must be exactly one certificate, with its inner and outer signat"
    "ure algorithms equal. UTCTime years\n    50 to 99 are read as 19xx. An unknown key or signature algor"
    "ithm still parses, as `UnsupportedKey` or\n    `UnsupportedSignature`; an unknown critical extension "
    "sets `unhandled_critical`. An Ed25519 key or\n    signature algorithm (OID 1.3.101.112) is `Ed25519Ke"
    "y` or `Ed25519`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}certificates_from_pem\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn certificates_from_pem(StringView tex"
    "t) : Vec<Certificate>\u{1f}Every certificate in the PEM `text`, in order: its `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE----"
    "-` blocks (RFC 7468).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn certificates_from_pem(StringView text) : Vec<Certificate>\n    in `s"
    "td::x509`\n\n    Every certificate in the PEM `text`, in order: its `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----` bloc"
    "ks (RFC 7468).\n\n    Text between blocks is ignored. A block whose base64 does not decode, that holds"
    " a byte that is not ASCII,\n    or that is not a certificate, is skipped.\n\n    Example, \"certificates"
    "_from_pem: a malformed block is skipped\":\n        StringView text = \"junk\\n-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE---"
    "--\\nnot base64!\\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----\\n\";\n        Vec<Certificate> certs = certificates_from_pe"
    "m(text);\n        assert(Vec::len(&certs) == 0);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}TrustStore\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct TrustSto"
    "re\u{1f}The root certificates a chain may end at, for `verify_chain`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct TrustStore\n    in `s"
    "td::x509`\n\n    The root certificates a chain may end at, for `verify_chain`.\n\n    `roots` may be rea"
    "d and changed directly; `TrustStore::system` reads the operating system's.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}TrustStore::n"
    "ew\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::new() : TrustStore\u{1f}A store with no roots.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::new() :"
    " TrustStore\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    A store with no roots.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}TrustStore::add\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn "
    "TrustStore::add(ref<TrustStore, exclusive> t, Certificate root)\u{1f}Adds `root` to the roots of `t`.\u{1f}\u{1f}ex"
    "port fn TrustStore::add(ref<TrustStore, exclusive> t, Certificate root)\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    Adds"
    " `root` to the roots of `t`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}TrustStore::from_pem_file\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::from_pem"
    "_file(StringView path) : Result<TrustStore, FileError>\u{1f}The roots in the PEM file at `path`, such as "
    "`/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::from_pem_file(StringView path) : Result"
    "<TrustStore, FileError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The roots in the PEM file at `path`, such as `/etc/s"
    "sl/certs/ca-certificates.crt`.\n\n    Its certificates are read as `certificates_from_pem` reads them."
    " `Err` with the `FileError` when the file\n    cannot be read.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}TrustStore::system\u{1f}fn\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn TrustStore::system() : Result<TrustStore, FileError>\u{1f}The operating system's roots, from the fi"
    "rst of the usual bundle files that holds a certificate.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TrustStore::system() : Result<Tru"
    "stStore, FileError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The operating system's roots, from the first of the usua"
    "l bundle files that holds a certificate.\n\n    The files tried, in order: `/etc/ssl/certs/ca-certific"
    "ates.crt` (Debian, Ubuntu),\n    `/etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt` (Fedora, RHEL), `/etc/ssl/ca-bund"
    "le.pem`, `/etc/ssl/cert.pem` (Alpine)\n    and `/usr/local/etc/openssl/cert.pem` (macOS with a packag"
    "e manager's OpenSSL). `Err(NotFound)` where none\n    does, as on Windows: a program there passes a b"
    "undle to `TrustStore::from_pem_file`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}verify_signature\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn verify_signature(ref"
    "<CertKey, shared> key, ref<SignatureScheme, shared> scheme, slice<u8, shared> message, slice<u8, sha"
    "red> signature) : bool\u{1f}Whether `signature` over `message` verifies under `key` with `scheme`.\u{1f}\u{1f}expor"
    "t fn verify_signature(ref<CertKey, shared> key, ref<SignatureScheme, shared> scheme, slice<u8, share"
    "d> message, slice<u8, shared> signature) : bool\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    Whether `signature` over `me"
    "ssage` verifies under `key` with `scheme`.\n\n    The RSA and ECDSA schemes hash `message` with the sc"
    "heme's hash first; Ed25519 checks `message` itself. A\n    key of another kind than the scheme, `Unsu"
    "pportedKey`, `UnsupportedSignature` or a malformed signature\n    gives `false`. Not constant-time, a"
    "nd need not be: it uses public values only.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}Certificate::matches_host\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Certi"
    "ficate::matches_host(ref<Certificate, shared> c, StringView host) : bool\u{1f}Whether `c` is for `host` ("
    "RFC 6125 §6.4).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Certificate::matches_host(ref<Certificate, shared> c, StringView host) :"
    " bool\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    Whether `c` is for `host` (RFC 6125 §6.4).\n\n    An IP address literal"
    " is compared with the certificate's IP addresses. A name is compared with its DNS\n    names, ignorin"
    "g ASCII case and one final dot on `host`; a leading `*.` in a DNS name stands for exactly\n    one wh"
    "ole label, and only where at least two labels follow it (so `*.com` matches nothing). The common\n   "
    " name is not consulted.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}verify_chain\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn verify_chain(ref<Certificate, shared> "
    "leaf, slice<Certificate, shared> intermediates, ref<TrustStore, shared> roots, StringView host, ref<"
    "DateTime, shared> now) : Result<void, CertError>\u{1f}Verifies a TLS server's certificate chain from `lea"
    "f` to one of `roots`, for `host` at the time `now`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn verify_chain(ref<Certificate, shared>"
    " leaf, slice<Certificate, shared> intermediates, ref<TrustStore, shared> roots, StringView host, ref"
    "<DateTime, shared> now) : Result<void, CertError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    Verifies a TLS server's ce"
    "rtificate chain from `leaf` to one of `roots`, for `host` at the time `now`.\n\n    `Ok(())` when the "
    "leaf matches `host` (`Certificate::matches_host`), may serve TLS, is in date and usable,\n    and a c"
    "hain of at most 10 certificates exists (RFC 5280 §6, as a client needs it) in which:\n\n    - each ce"
    "rtificate is signed by the next, found by issuer name and signature among `intermediates`, in any\n  "
    "    order, or among the roots;\n    - every issuer is a CA allowed to sign certificates, in date, and"
    " within its path length;\n    - the last is one of the roots.\n\n    Otherwise `Err` of the first reaso"
    "n met: `HostMismatch`, then `WrongUsage`, then `NotYetValid`, `Expired`\n    or `UnhandledCritical` f"
    "or the leaf, then the chain's (`UnknownAuthority`, `BadSignature`, `NotAuthority`,\n    `NotYetValid`"
    ", `Expired`, `UnhandledCritical` or `ChainTooLong`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}CertKey::to_der\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CertKe"
    "y::to_der(ref<CertKey, shared> key) : Option<Vec<u8>>\u{1f}The DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo of `key`, or `Non"
    "e` for `UnsupportedKey`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CertKey::to_der(ref<CertKey, shared> key) : Option<Vec<u8>>\n    "
    "in `std::x509`\n\n    The DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo of `key`, or `None` for `UnsupportedKey`.\n\n    `Cer"
    "tKey::from_der` reads it back.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}CertKey::from_der\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CertKey::from_der(slice<u8"
    ", shared> der) : Result<CertKey, CertError>\u{1f}The public key of the DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo `der`.\u{1f}\u{1f}e"
    "xport fn CertKey::from_der(slice<u8, shared> der) : Result<CertKey, CertError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n "
    "   The public key of the DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo `der`.\n\n    `Err(BadEncoding)` when `der` is not e"
    "xactly one SubjectPublicKeyInfo; `Err(UnsupportedAlgorithm)` when\n    its algorithm is not RSA, P-25"
    "6, P-384 or Ed25519.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}CertKey::from_pem\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CertKey::from_pem(StringView text) :"
    " Result<CertKey, CertError>\u{1f}The public key of the first `-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----` block in `text`"
    " (RFC 7468).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CertKey::from_pem(StringView text) : Result<CertKey, CertError>\n    in `std:"
    ":x509`\n\n    The public key of the first `-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----` block in `text` (RFC 7468).\n\n  "
    "  The block's DER is read as `CertKey::from_der` reads it; `Err(BadEncoding)` when there is no such "
    "block,\n    or its base64 does not decode.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}CertKey::to_pem\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CertKey::to_pem(r"
    "ef<CertKey, shared> key) : Option<String>\u{1f}`key` as a PEM `PUBLIC KEY` block of 64-character lines, o"
    "r `None` for `UnsupportedKey`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CertKey::to_pem(ref<CertKey, shared> key) : Option<String>"
    "\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    `key` as a PEM `PUBLIC KEY` block of 64-character lines, or `None` for `Uns"
    "upportedKey`.\n\n    Example, \"CertKey::to_pem: read back by from_pem\":\n        CertKey key = Ed25519K"
    "ey([0x42; 32]);\n        String pem = Option::unwrap(CertKey::to_pem(&key));\n        assert(StringVie"
    "w::starts_with(&pem, \"-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\\n\"));\n        match (CertKey::from_pem(&pem))\n     "
    "   {\n            Ok(Ed25519Key(k)) : assert(k[0] == 0x42 && k[31] == 0x42),\n            _           "
    "      : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}EcPrivateKey\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct EcPrivateKey\u{1f}An ellip"
    "tic-curve private key: the curve and the scalar, 32 bytes for P-256 or 48 for P-384.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct "
    "EcPrivateKey\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    An elliptic-curve private key: the curve and the scalar, 32 byt"
    "es for P-256 or 48 for P-384.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}PrivateKey\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum PrivateKey\u{1f}A private key of on"
    "e of the algorithms `std` signs with.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum PrivateKey\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    A private key "
    "of one of the algorithms `std` signs with.\n\n    - `RsaPrivate`: an RSA key.\n    - `EcPrivate`: a P-2"
    "56 or P-384 key.\n    - `Ed25519Private`: an Ed25519 key, its 32-byte private key (the seed).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::"
    "x509\u{1f}PrivateKey::public_key\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::public_key(ref<PrivateKey, shared> key) : CertK"
    "ey\u{1f}The public key that matches `key`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::public_key(ref<PrivateKey, shared> key)"
    " : CertKey\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The public key that matches `key`.\n\n    An EC key whose scalar do"
    "es not name a number in [1, n-1], which `PrivateKey::from_der` never gives, gets\n    an empty point;"
    " a scalar of the wrong length faults (`crypto_length`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}PrivateKey::from_der\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export f"
    "n PrivateKey::from_der(slice<u8, shared> der) : Result<PrivateKey, CertError>\u{1f}The private key of the"
    " DER `der`: a PKCS #8 PrivateKeyInfo (RFC 5958), PKCS #1 RSAPrivateKey or SEC 1 ECPrivateKey.\u{1f}\u{1f}expor"
    "t fn PrivateKey::from_der(slice<u8, shared> der) : Result<PrivateKey, CertError>\n    in `std::x509`\n"
    "\n    The private key of the DER `der`: a PKCS #8 PrivateKeyInfo (RFC 5958), PKCS #1 RSAPrivateKey or"
    " SEC 1\n    ECPrivateKey.\n\n    The three are told apart by their first fields; a SEC 1 key's curve co"
    "mes from its own parameters. The\n    numbers are checked as `RsaPrivateKey::new` and `ec_public_key`"
    " check them. `Err(BadEncoding)` when `der`\n    is none of these or its numbers do not fit together; "
    "`Err(UnsupportedAlgorithm)` for an algorithm or curve\n    `std` does not sign with.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}Priv"
    "ateKey::to_der\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::to_der(ref<PrivateKey, shared> key) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}`key` as DER P"
    "KCS #8 (version 0), which `PrivateKey::from_der` reads back.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::to_der(ref<Priva"
    "teKey, shared> key) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    `key` as DER PKCS #8 (version 0), which `Priva"
    "teKey::from_der` reads back.\n\n    An RSA key with its Chinese-remainder values, an EC key with its p"
    "ublic key, an Ed25519 key as its seed.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}PrivateKey::from_pem\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::fro"
    "m_pem(StringView text) : Result<PrivateKey, CertError>\u{1f}The private key of a `PRIVATE KEY`, `RSA PRIV"
    "ATE KEY` or `EC PRIVATE KEY` block in `text`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::from_pem(StringView text) : Res"
    "ult<PrivateKey, CertError>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    The private key of a `PRIVATE KEY`, `RSA PRIVATE "
    "KEY` or `EC PRIVATE KEY` block in `text`.\n\n    The block's DER is read as `PrivateKey::from_der` rea"
    "ds it. The labels are looked for in that order, so a\n    `PRIVATE KEY` block is taken even when a bl"
    "ock of the other kinds comes before it. An\n    `ENCRYPTED PRIVATE KEY` block alone is `Err(Unsupport"
    "edAlgorithm)`; no block, or base64 that does not\n    decode, is `Err(BadEncoding)`.\n\n    Example, \"P"
    "rivateKey::from_pem: an encrypted key is not read\":\n        StringView text = \"-----BEGIN ENCRYPTED "
    "PRIVATE KEY-----\\nAAAA\\n-----END ENCRYPTED PRIVATE KEY-----\\n\";\n        match (PrivateKey::from_pem("
    "text))\n        {\n            Err(UnsupportedAlgorithm) : assert(true),\n            _                "
    "         : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}PrivateKey::to_pem\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::to_pem(r"
    "ef<PrivateKey, shared> key) : String\u{1f}`key` as a PEM `PRIVATE KEY` block (PKCS #8) of 64-character li"
    "nes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PrivateKey::to_pem(ref<PrivateKey, shared> key) : String\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    `ke"
    "y` as a PEM `PRIVATE KEY` block (PKCS #8) of 64-character lines.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::x509\u{1f}sign\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn sign("
    "ref<PrivateKey, shared> key, ref<SignatureScheme, shared> scheme, slice<u8, shared> message) : Optio"
    "n<Vec<u8>>\u{1f}`key`'s signature of `message` under `scheme`, which `verify_signature` accepts with the "
    "matching public key.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn sign(ref<PrivateKey, shared> key, ref<SignatureScheme, shared> schem"
    "e, slice<u8, shared> message) : Option<Vec<u8>>\n    in `std::x509`\n\n    `key`'s signature of `messag"
    "e` under `scheme`, which `verify_signature` accepts with the matching public\n    key.\n\n    The RSA P"
    "KCS #1 v1.5, RSA-PSS and ECDSA schemes sign the scheme's hash of `message`; Ed25519 signs\n    `messa"
    "ge` whole. `None` when `key` is not of the scheme's kind, the scheme is `UnsupportedSignature`, or\n "
    "   an EC key's scalar is not in [1, n-1]. An RSA modulus too short for the scheme's hash faults\n    "
    "(`crypto_length`).\n\n    Example, \"sign: a key of another kind gives None\":\n        PrivateKey key = "
    "Ed25519Private([1; 32]);\n        SignatureScheme scheme = RsaPss(Sha2_256);\n        assert(Option::i"
    "s_none(&sign(&key, &scheme, b\"message\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsError\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum TlsError\u{1f}Why a TLS c"
    "onnection failed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum TlsError\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    Why a TLS connection failed.\n\n    - `"
    "TlsNetFailure(e)`: the socket failed as `e` says; also a line `read_line` read that is not UTF-8\n   "
    "   (`NotUtf8`), and a `read_exact` cut short (`Closed`).\n    - `CertRejected(e)`: the server's certi"
    "ficate chain did not verify, as `e` says.\n    - `HandshakeFailed`: a negotiation this side cannot co"
    "mplete.\n    - `ProtocolError`: the peer sent a malformed message.\n    - `PeerAlert(code)`: the peer "
    "sent an alert with this description code (40 handshake_failure, 70\n      protocol_version, and so on"
    ").\n    - `RecordRejected`: a record did not authenticate.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsError::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Tls"
    "Error::text(ref<TlsError, shared> e) : str\u{1f}A one-line description of the error, for messages; the co"
    "mmon alert codes are named.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsError::text(ref<TlsError, shared> e) : str\n    in `std::tl"
    "s`\n\n    A one-line description of the error, for messages; the common alert codes are named.\n\n    Ex"
    "ample, \"TlsError::text: alerts and network failures\":\n        TlsError e = PeerAlert(70);\n        as"
    "sert(TlsError::text(&e) == \"the peer does not speak TLS 1.3 (alert 70)\");\n        TlsError n = TlsNe"
    "tFailure(Refused);\n        assert(TlsError::text(&n) == \"connection refused\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream\u{1f}"
    "struct\u{1f}export resource struct TlsStream\u{1f}A TLS 1.3 connection over a `TcpStream`, as a client (`clien"
    "t`, `connect`) or as a server (`server`).\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct TlsStream\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    A"
    " TLS 1.3 connection over a `TcpStream`, as a client (`client`, `connect`) or as a server (`server`)."
    "\n\n    It speaks the cipher suites TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256, TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 and\n    TLS_A"
    "ES_256_GCM_SHA384, the key exchanges X25519, P-256 and P-384, and ECDSA, RSA-PSS and Ed25519\n    sig"
    "natures. No TLS 1.2, no session resumption, no early data, no client certificates. Dropping the\n    "
    "stream closes the connection without close_notify; `close` sends it first.\n\n    Implemented to RFC 8"
    "446, tested against its vectors and against OpenSSL on loopback, and fuzzed\n    continuously; not in"
    "dependently audited.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::peer_certificate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::peer_certificate"
    "(ref<TlsStream, shared> s) : Option<ref<Certificate, shared>>\u{1f}The peer's certificate that the handsh"
    "ake verified: on a client's stream, the server's leaf.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::peer_certificate(ref<Tl"
    "sStream, shared> s) : Option<ref<Certificate, shared>>\n    in `std::tls`\n\n    The peer's certificate"
    " that the handshake verified: on a client's stream, the server's leaf.\n\n    `None` on a server's str"
    "eam, since clients send none. A program that pins a key or a certificate\n    compares it here.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std"
    "::tls\u{1f}TlsStream::peer_addr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TlsStream::peer_addr(ref<TlsStream, shared> s) : SocketAddr\u{1f}"
