    "::http\u{1f}Url\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Url\u{1f}A parsed absolute URL, `scheme://host[:port]/path?query`.\u{1f}\u{1f}expor"
    "t struct Url\n    in `std::http`\n\n    A parsed absolute URL, `scheme://host[:port]/path?query`.\n\n    "
    "- `scheme`: lower-cased.\n    - `host`: lower-cased; an IPv6 host keeps its brackets (`[::1]`).\n    -"
    " `port`: the number after the host's `:`, or the scheme's default: 443 for `https`, 80 otherwise.\n  "
    "  - `path`: \"/\" when the text has none.\n    - `query`: the text after `?`, without it; empty when th"
    "ere is none.\n\n    The fragment (`#…`), which never reaches a server, is dropped.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url::"
    "parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Url::parse(StringView text) : Result<Url, HttpError>\u{1f}Parses an absolute URL.\u{1f}\u{1f}exp"
    "ort fn Url::parse(StringView text) : Result<Url, HttpError>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    Parses an absolu"
    "te URL.\n\n    `Err(BadUrl)` for text without `://`, with an empty host part, with user information (`"
    "user@`), or with\n    a port that is not a number up to 65535. The scheme is not checked here: `HttpC"
    "lient::send` gives\n    `Err(UnsupportedScheme)` for one that is neither `http` nor `https`.\n\n    Exa"
    "mple, \"Url::parse: defaults and normalisation\":\n        Url u = Result::unwrap(Url::parse(\"HTTPS://E"
    "xample.com/a/b?x=1#top\"));\n        assert(u.scheme == \"https\" && u.host == \"example.com\" && u.port ="
    "= 443);\n        assert(u.path == \"/a/b\" && u.query == \"x=1\");\n        assert(Url::target(&u) == \"/a/"
    "b?x=1\");\n        Url v = Result::unwrap(Url::parse(\"http://[::1]:8080\"));\n        assert(v.host == \""
    "[::1]\" && v.path == \"/\");\n        assert(Url::text(&v) == \"http://[::1]:8080/\");\n        assert(Resu"
    "lt::is_err(&Url::parse(\"http://user@example.com/\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url::target\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Url::targ"
    "et(ref<Url, shared> u) : String\u{1f}The request target: the path, then `?` and the query when the query "
    "is not empty.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Url::target(ref<Url, shared> u) : String\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The reques"
    "t target: the path, then `?` and the query when the query is not empty.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Url::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}exp"
