    "pped by `Url::parse`, does not come back.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}percent_encode\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn percent_encode(sli"
    "ce<u8, shared> bytes) : String\u{1f}Percent-encodes `bytes` as RFC 3986 does: unreserved bytes as they ar"
    "e, every other as `%XX`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn percent_encode(slice<u8, shared> bytes) : String\n    in `std::ht"
    "tp`\n\n    Percent-encodes `bytes` as RFC 3986 does: unreserved bytes as they are, every other as `%XX"
    "`.\n\n    The unreserved bytes are ASCII letters and digits, `-`, `.`, `_` and `~`; the hex digits are"
    " upper\n    case. A space becomes `%20`; `form_encode` writes it as `+`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}percent_decode\u{1f}f"
    "n\u{1f}export fn percent_decode(StringView text) : Option<Vec<u8>>\u{1f}The bytes `text` percent-encodes, each"
    " `%XX` decoded.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn percent_decode(StringView text) : Option<Vec<u8>>\n    in `std::http`\n\n   "
    " The bytes `text` percent-encodes, each `%XX` decoded.\n\n    `None` for a `%` not followed by two hex"
    " digits; hex digits of either case are read. A `+` stays\n    a `+`; `form_decode` reads it as a spac"
    "e.\n\n    Example, \"percent_decode: the reverse of percent_encode\":\n        assert(percent_encode(Stri"
    "ngView::as_bytes(\"a b/ü\")) == \"a%20b%2F%C3%BC\");\n        Vec<u8> back = Option::unwrap(percent_deco"
    "de(\"a%20b%2f\"));\n        assert(Result::unwrap(String::from_utf8(back)) == \"a b/\");\n        assert(O"
    "ption::is_none(&percent_decode(\"100%\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Param\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Param\u{1f}One name and "
    "value of a query string or an `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` body.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Param\n    in "
    "`std::http`\n\n    One name and value of a query string or an `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` body"
    ".\n\n    Names compare exactly (`find_param`), unlike a header's.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Param::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn "
