    "ed> headers, StringView name) : Option<StringView> from headers\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The value of"
    " the first header named `name`, ignoring ASCII case, or `None` when there is none.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Reque"
    "st\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Request\u{1f}An HTTP request: the method, the URL, the headers and the body.\u{1f}\u{1f}exp"
    "ort struct Request\n    in `std::http`\n\n    An HTTP request: the method, the URL, the headers and the"
    " body.\n\n    For the client, `url` is absolute (`https://…`); for a request a server received, it i"
    "s the target as\n    sent (`/path?query`). A server's request has the body decoded if it came chunked"
