    "<StringView> from r\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The value of the response's first header named `name`, i"
    "gnoring ASCII case.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}Response::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Response::text(ref<Response, shared> r) "
    ": Result<String, Utf8Error>\u{1f}The body as text: a copy of its bytes, which must be UTF-8.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn R"
    "esponse::text(ref<Response, shared> r) : Result<String, Utf8Error>\n    in `std::http`\n\n    The body "
    "as text: a copy of its bytes, which must be UTF-8.\n\n    `Err(e)` when they are not.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http\u{1f}reas"
    "on_phrase\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn reason_phrase(u16 status) : str\u{1f}The reason phrase RFC 9110 gives a status cod"
    "e, such as \"Not Found\" for 404.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn reason_phrase(u16 status) : str\n    in `std::http`\n\n    T"
    "he reason phrase RFC 9110 gives a status code, such as \"Not Found\" for 404.\n\n    \"\" for a status it "
    "does not list here.\n\n    Example, \"reason_phrase: unlisted codes\":\n        assert(reason_phrase(404)"
    " == \"Not Found\");\n        assert(reason_phrase(299) == \"\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}HttpClient\u{1f}struct\u{1f}ex"
    "port struct HttpClient\u{1f}An HTTP/1.1 client: the settings and the state it carries from request to req"
    "uest.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct HttpClient\n    in `std::http::client`\n\n    An HTTP/1.1 client: the settings and"
    " the state it carries from request to request.\n\n    - `roots`: the trusted roots https verifies serv"
    "ers against; `None` until the first https request\n      loads the system's (`TrustStore::system`), o"
    "r a store the program puts there.\n    - `timeout_ms`: the timeout for connecting and for each read a"
    "nd write, in milliseconds.\n    - `max_redirects`: how many redirects `send` follows.\n    - `max_body"
    "`: the most bytes a response body may have, after decompression too (`TooLarge` beyond).\n    - `head"
    "ers`: sent with every request; a request's own header of the same name replaces one.\n    - `keep_ali"
    "ve`: when set, the last connection is kept open while the server allows, and the next\n      request "
    "to the same origin goes on it; when not (the default), each request has its own connection.\n\n    A p"
    "rogram that makes several https requests keeps one client, so the roots are loaded once.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http"
    "::client\u{1f}HttpClient::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpClient::new() : HttpClient\u{1f}A client with the default setti"
    "ngs.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpClient::new() : HttpClient\n    in `std::http::client`\n\n    A client with the def"
    "ault settings.\n\n    No roots loaded yet, a 30 s timeout, up to 10 redirects, a 16 MiB body limit, `k"
    "eep_alive` off, and\n    the headers `User-Agent` and `Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate`.\n\n    Example,"
    " \"HttpClient::new: the defaults\":\n        HttpClient c = HttpClient::new();\n        assert(c.timeout"
    "_ms == 30000 && c.max_redirects == 10 && !c.keep_alive);\n        assert(Option::is_none(&c.roots));\n"
    "        assert(Option::is_some(&find_header(&c.headers, \"user-agent\")));\n        c.max_body = 1_048_"
    "576;\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}HttpClient::send\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpClient::send(ref<HttpClient, exclusive> c"
    ", ref<Request, shared> req) : Result<Response, HttpError>\u{1f}Sends `req` and gives the final response, "
    "following redirects.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpClient::send(ref<HttpClient, exclusive> c, ref<Request, shared> "
    "req) : Result<Response, HttpError>\n    in `std::http::client`\n\n    Sends `req` and gives the final r"
    "esponse, following redirects.\n\n    - `req.url` is absolute; a scheme other than `http` or `https` is"
    " `Err(UnsupportedScheme)`. The\n      host's addresses are tried in turn.\n    - The request carries `"
    "Host`, the client's headers and then the request's own (`Host`,\n      `Content-Length` and `Connecti"
    "on` of the request are ignored), `Content-Length` when the body is not\n      empty or the method is "
    "POST, PUT or PATCH, and `Connection: close` unless `keep_alive` is set.\n    - Interim responses (sta"
    "tus 1xx) are read past. A body sent with `Content-Encoding: gzip` or `deflate`\n      arrives decoded"
    ".\n    - A 301, 302 or 303 with a `Location` is followed by GET without the body (HEAD stays HEAD), a"
    " 307 or\n      308 with the method and body kept; a redirect without `Location` is given as it is. On"
    "e redirect\n      more than `max_redirects` is `Err(TooManyRedirects)`. Once a redirect leaves the re"
    "quest's origin\n      (scheme, host and port), `Authorization`, `Proxy-Authorization` and `Cookie`, t"
    "he client's and the\n      request's, are not sent again.\n    - On a kept connection that proves clos"
    "ed before any of the response arrives, an idempotent request\n      (GET, HEAD, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS,"
    " TRACE) is sent again on a fresh connection; another is\n      `Err(ConnectionClosed)`, since the ser"
    "ver may have acted on it.\n    - Network and TLS failures are `Err(HttpNetFailure(e))` and `Err(HttpT"
    "lsFailure(e))`; see `HttpError`\n      for the rest.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}http_get\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn http_g"
    "et(StringView url) : Result<Response, HttpError>\u{1f}Sends a GET of `url` with a fresh `HttpClient::new("
    ")` and gives the response.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn http_get(StringView url) : Result<Response, HttpError>\n    in "
    "`std::http::client`\n\n    Sends a GET of `url` with a fresh `HttpClient::new()` and gives the respons"
    "e.\n\n    For https each call loads the system's roots again; a program that makes several requests ke"
    "eps an\n    `HttpClient`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::client\u{1f}http_post\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn http_post(StringView url, String"
    "View content_type, slice<u8, shared> body) : Result<Response, HttpError>\u{1f}Sends a POST of `body` to `"
    "url`, with `Content-Type: content_type`, from a fresh default client.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn http_post(StringVie"
    "w url, StringView content_type, slice<u8, shared> body) : Result<Response, HttpError>\n    in `std::h"
    "ttp::client`\n\n    Sends a POST of `body` to `url`, with `Content-Type: content_type`, from a fresh d"
    "efault client.\n\n    As `http_get`, a program that makes several requests keeps an `HttpClient`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}st"
    "d::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct HttpServer\u{1f}A listening HTTP/1.1 server: `ac"
    "cept` gives each client's connection.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resource struct HttpServer\n    in `std::http::server`\n"
    "\n    A listening HTTP/1.1 server: `accept` gives each client's connection.\n\n    - `max_body`: the mo"
    "st bytes a request body may have (`TooLarge` beyond); 16 MiB from `bind`.\n    - `timeout_ms`: the ti"
    "meout for each read and write on the connections it accepts, in milliseconds;\n      30 s from `bind`"
    ".\n\n    The limits apply to every connection accepted after they are set. A server program handles ea"
    "ch\n    connection in a thread of its own (`spawn`). Dropping the server closes its listening socket."
    "\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer::bind\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::bind(SocketAddr a) : Result<HttpServe"
    "r, NetError>\u{1f}An HTTP server listening at `a`, with a 16 MiB body limit and a 30 s timeout per read a"
    "nd write.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::bind(SocketAddr a) : Result<HttpServer, NetError>\n    in `std::http"
    "::server`\n\n    An HTTP server listening at `a`, with a 16 MiB body limit and a 30 s timeout per read"
    " and write.\n\n    Port 0 asks the system for a free port (`local_addr` names it). Errors as `TcpListe"
    "ner::bind`'s.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer::bind_tls\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::bind_tls(SocketAddr "
    "a, PrivateKey key, Vec<Certificate> chain) : Result<HttpServer, NetError>\u{1f}An HTTPS server listening "
    "at `a`: each connection it accepts first completes a TLS 1.3 handshake.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::bind_"
    "tls(SocketAddr a, PrivateKey key, Vec<Certificate> chain) : Result<HttpServer, NetError>\n    in `std"
    "::http::server`\n\n    An HTTPS server listening at `a`: each connection it accepts first completes a "
    "TLS 1.3 handshake.\n\n    `key` is the server's private key and `chain` its certificate first, then it"
    "s issuers, as\n    `TlsStream::server` takes them. Otherwise as `bind`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServe"
    "r::local_addr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::local_addr(ref<HttpServer, shared> s) : SocketAddr\u{1f}The addres"
    "s the server listens at, with the port the system chose for port 0.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServer::local_add"
    "r(ref<HttpServer, shared> s) : SocketAddr\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    The address the server lis"
    "tens at, with the port the system chose for port 0.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpServer::accept\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export"
    " fn HttpServer::accept(ref<HttpServer, exclusive> s) : Result<HttpConnection, HttpError>\u{1f}Waits for t"
    "he next client and gives its connection, with the server's limits and timeouts.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpServe"
    "r::accept(ref<HttpServer, exclusive> s) : Result<HttpConnection, HttpError>\n    in `std::http::serve"
    "r`\n\n    Waits for the next client and gives its connection, with the server's limits and timeouts.\n\n"
    "    For an https server the TLS handshake comes first: a client that fails it is `Err(HttpTlsFailure"
    "(e))`,\n    and the server is ready for the next. A failure of the listener is `Err(HttpNetFailure(e)"
    ")`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpConnection\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export resource struct HttpConnection\u{1f}One client's con"
    "nection to an `HttpServer`: `request`, then `respond`, repeated while it stays open.\u{1f}\u{1f}export resourc"
    "e struct HttpConnection\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    One client's connection to an `HttpServer`: "
    "`request`, then `respond`, repeated while it stays open.\n\n    The connection stays open for the next"
    " request when the request is HTTP/1.1 without\n    `Connection: close`, or HTTP/1.0 with `Connection:"
    " keep-alive`. Dropping it closes the socket; `close`\n    ends it cleanly first.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}"
    "HttpConnection::peer_addr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::peer_addr(ref<HttpConnection, shared> c) : So"
    "cketAddr\u{1f}The client's address.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::peer_addr(ref<HttpConnection, shared> c) :"
    " SocketAddr\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    The client's address.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpConnection"
    "::request\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::request(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c) : Result<Option<Req"
    "uest>, HttpError>\u{1f}Reads the client's next request, or gives `None` when there is none to read.\u{1f}\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn HttpConnection::request(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c) : Result<Option<Request>, HttpError>"
    "\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    Reads the client's next request, or gives `None` when there is none"
    " to read.\n\n    - `Ok(Some(r))`: `r.url` is the target as sent (`/path?query`); the body is read by `"
    "Content-Length` or\n      chunked encoding, and there is none without them. When the request expects "
    "`100-continue`, the\n      `HTTP/1.1 100 Continue` is sent before the body is read.\n    - `Ok(None)`:"
    " the client closed before a request, or the last response ended the connection.\n    - `Err(BadMessag"
    "e)`: a malformed request line (a control byte in the target), header or body, an HTTP/1.1\n      requ"
    "est without `Host`, a request with two `Host` fields, or `Content-Length` fields that disagree;\n    "
    "  `Err(TooLarge)`: a head over 65536 bytes or a body over `max_body`. The caller answers 400 or 413 "
    "if\n      it wishes, and the connection then closes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpConnection::respond\u{1f}fn\u{1f}e"
    "xport fn HttpConnection::respond(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c, u16 status, slice<Header, shared>"
    " headers, slice<u8, shared> body) : Result<void, HttpError>\u{1f}Writes a response with `status`, `header"
    "s` and `body`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::respond(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c, u16 status, slic"
    "e<Header, shared> headers, slice<u8, shared> body) : Result<void, HttpError>\n    in `std::http::serv"
    "er`\n\n    Writes a response with `status`, `headers` and `body`.\n\n    The status line carries `reason"
    "_phrase(status)`. `Content-Length` and `Connection` among `headers` are\n    dropped: `Content-Length"
    "` is written from `body` (not for 1xx, 204 or 304), and `Connection` as\n    negotiated. The body is "
    "left out after a HEAD request and for a status that has none. After a response\n    that ends the con"
    "nection, the connection is closed and `request` gives `None`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::http::server\u{1f}HttpConnection::cl"
    "ose\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::close(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c)\u{1f}Ends the connection: closes"
    " its sending side, or sends TLS's close_notify on an https connection.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn HttpConnection::cl"
    "ose(ref<HttpConnection, exclusive> c)\n    in `std::http::server`\n\n    Ends the connection: closes it"
    "s sending side, or sends TLS's close_notify on an https connection.\n\n    Does nothing on a connectio"
    "n already closed.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}scram_salted_password\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn scram_salted_password(StringVie"
    "w password, slice<u8, shared> salt, usize iterations) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}The SCRAM-SHA-256 salted password: P"
    "BKDF2 over HMAC-SHA-256 of `password` and `salt`, 32 bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn scram_salted_password(StringV"
    "iew password, slice<u8, shared> salt, usize iterations) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::database`\n\n    The SC"
    "RAM-SHA-256 salted password: PBKDF2 over HMAC-SHA-256 of `password` and `salt`, 32 bytes.\n\n    `iter"
    "ations` is the server's count. The password is used as given, with no SASLprep normalisation.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std:"
    ":database\u{1f}Scram\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct Scram\u{1f}The client's side of one SCRAM-SHA-256 exchange (RFC 5802"
    ", RFC 7677), without channel binding.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct Scram\n    in `std::database`\n\n    The client's "
    "side of one SCRAM-SHA-256 exchange (RFC 5802, RFC 7677), without channel binding.\n\n    The steps in "
    "order: `Scram::start`, send `Scram::client_first`, answer the server's first message with\n    `Scram"
    "::respond`, then check the server's final message with `Scram::verify`. The PostgreSQL client uses\n "
    "   it; it is exported so a program can speak the exchange to another server.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Scram::"
    "start\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Scram::start(StringView user, StringView client_nonce) : Scram\u{1f}A new exchange for"
    " `user` with the client's nonce `client_nonce`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::start(StringView user, StringView "
    "client_nonce) : Scram\n    in `std::database`\n\n    A new exchange for `user` with the client's nonce "
    "`client_nonce`.\n\n    `,` and `=` in `user` are escaped as `=2C` and `=3D`. The nonce should be fresh"
    " random text for each\n    exchange, such as the base64 of bytes from `os_random_bytes`. PostgreSQL i"
    "gnores the user, and its client\n    sends `\"\"`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Scram::client_first\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Scr"
    "am::client_first(ref<Scram, shared> s) : String\u{1f}The client's first message, `n,,n=USER,r=NONCE`: no "
    "channel binding.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::client_first(ref<Scram, shared> s) : String\n    in `std::database"
    "`\n\n    The client's first message, `n,,n=USER,r=NONCE`: no channel binding.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Scram::r"
    "espond\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Scram::respond(ref<Scram, exclusive> s, StringView server_first, StringView pass"
    "word) : Result<String, PgError>\u{1f}The client's final message, carrying the proof of `password`, for th"
    "e server's first message.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::respond(ref<Scram, exclusive> s, StringView server_first"
    ", StringView password) : Result<String, PgError>\n    in `std::database`\n\n    The client's final mess"
    "age, carrying the proof of `password`, for the server's first message.\n\n    `server_first` is the se"
    "rver's `r=…,s=…,i=…`. Remembers the signature `Scram::verify` then expects.\n    `Err(AuthFaile"
    "d)` when the server's nonce does not begin with the client's and add to it;\n    `Err(ProtocolViolati"
    "on)` when the message is malformed, asks for an extension (`m=`), gives an iteration\n    count of 0 "
    "or a salt that is not base64.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database\u{1f}Scram::verify\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Scram::verify(ref<Scram, sh"
    "ared> s, StringView server_final) : bool\u{1f}Whether the server's final message (`v=…`) carries the si"
    "gnature this exchange expects.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Scram::verify(ref<Scram, shared> s, StringView server_fina"
    "l) : bool\n    in `std::database`\n\n    Whether the server's final message (`v=…`) carries the signa"
    "ture this exchange expects.\n\n    `false` for anything else, an `e=` error among them, and `false` be"
    "fore `Scram::respond` has succeeded\n    (there is no signature to expect yet).\n\n    Example, \"Scram:"
    " a whole exchange\":\n        Scram s = Scram::start(\"user\", \"rOprNGfwEbeRWgbNEkqO\");\n        assert(S"
    "cram::client_first(&s) == \"n,,n=user,r=rOprNGfwEbeRWgbNEkqO\");\n        String first = \"r=rOprNGfwEbe"
    "RWgbNEkqO%hvYDpWUa2RaTCAfuxFIlj)hNlF$k0,\";\n        String::append(&mut first, \"s=W22ZaJ0SNY7soEsUEjb"
    "6gQ==,i=4\");\n        String reply = Result::unwrap(Scram::respond(&mut s, &first, \"pencil\"));\n      "
    "  assert(StringView::ends_with(&reply, \",p=0ByS2g6XZEtov8MR140MFRsEfy8/X+bacfpPofVtKjE=\"));\n        "
    "assert(Scram::verify(&s, \"v=ITrN4zX09+hsD398Qk6ol73eg0shWPnOWwnwS83jitc=\"));\n        assert(!Scram::"
    "verify(&s, \"e=invalid-proof\"));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgError\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum PgError\u{1f}Why a Pos"
    "tgreSQL connection or statement failed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum PgError\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    W"
    "hy a PostgreSQL connection or statement failed.\n\n    - `PgNetFailure(e)`: connecting, reading or wri"
    "ting failed; `e` says how.\n    - `PgTlsFailure(e)`: the TLS handshake or the encrypted stream failed"
    ".\n    - `TlsRefused`: the server does not accept TLS, and the URL asks for `verify-full`.\n    - `NoT"
    "rustedRoots`: the system's trusted roots could not be loaded.\n    - `BadConnectionUrl`: the URL is m"
    "alformed (`PgUrl::parse`).\n    - `UnsupportedAuth`: the server asks for a method other than SCRAM-SH"
    "A-256 or a password over TLS.\n    - `AuthRefused`: the server asks for the password in clear over an"
    " unencrypted connection.\n    - `AuthFailed`: the server refused the credentials, or failed to prove "
    "it knows them.\n    - `Server(e)`: the server reported an error; the connection stays usable.\n    - `"
    "ProtocolViolation`: a message from the server is malformed or not allowed at that point.\n    - `Resu"
    "ltTooLarge`: the rows exceed `max_result`, or more than 65 535 parameters were given.\n    - `Disconn"
    "ected`: the stream ended, or the connection was closed or broken by an earlier failure.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::datab"
    "ase::postgres\u{1f}PgServerError\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct PgServerError\u{1f}An error or notice the server reporte"
    "d.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct PgServerError\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    An error or notice the server "
    "reported.\n\n    `severity` is `ERROR`, `FATAL`, `NOTICE` and so on; `code` the five-character SQLSTAT"
    "E; `message` the\n    text; `detail`, `hint` and `position` (a character position from 1 into the sta"
    "tement) when the server\n    gave them.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgError::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgError:"
    ":text(ref<PgError, shared> e) : String\u{1f}`e` as text for a message; a server error as `severity: messa"
    "ge (code)`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgError::text(ref<PgError, shared> e) : String\n    in `std::database::postgre"
    "s`\n\n    `e` as text for a message; a server error as `severity: message (code)`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::po"
    "stgres\u{1f}PgSslMode\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum PgSslMode\u{1f}Whether a connection is encrypted.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum PgSslMod"
    "e\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    Whether a connection is encrypted.\n\n    - `Disable`: not enc"
    "rypted.\n    - `VerifyFull`: TLS, with the server's certificate verified for the host name against th"
    "e trusted roots.\n\n    An unverified TLS connection is not offered.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgUrl\u{1f}s"
    "truct\u{1f}export struct PgUrl\u{1f}A parsed connection URL, `postgres://user[:password]@host[:port]/database["
    "?sslmode=MODE]`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct PgUrl\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    A parsed connection URL,"
    " `postgres://user[:password]@host[:port]/database[?sslmode=MODE]`.\n\n    `user`, `password` and `data"
    "base` are percent-decoded; `host` is a name, an IPv4 literal or an IPv6\n    literal without its brac"
    "kets.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgUrl::parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgUrl::parse(StringView text) : Result<PgU"
    "rl, PgError>\u{1f}The connection URL `text` taken apart.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgUrl::parse(StringView text) : Resul"
    "t<PgUrl, PgError>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    The connection URL `text` taken apart.\n\n    "
    "The scheme is `postgres` or `postgresql`. The port defaults to 5432, the database to the user, `sslm"
    "ode`\n    to `verify-full`; the only query key is `sslmode`, `disable` or `verify-full`. `Err(BadConn"
    "ectionUrl)` for\n    another scheme, no user, no host, a port that is not a number, another query key"
    " or mode, or a bad\n    percent-encoding.\n\n    Example, \"PgUrl::parse: decoding and defaults\":\n      "
    "  PgUrl u = Result::unwrap(PgUrl::parse(\"postgres://app:p%40ss@[::1]/?sslmode=disable\"));\n        as"
    "sert(u.host == \"::1\" && u.port == 5432);\n        assert(u.database == \"app\");\n        match (&u.pass"
    "word)\n        {\n            Some(p) : assert(*p == \"p@ss\"),\n            None    : assert(false),\n   "
    "     }\n        Result<PgUrl, PgError> no_user = PgUrl::parse(\"postgres://db.example/shop\");\n        "
    "assert(Result::is_err(&no_user));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgValue\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum PgValue\u{1f}A state"
    "ment parameter, sent in the text form the server reads for it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum PgValue\n    in `std::dat"
    "abase::postgres`\n\n    A statement parameter, sent in the text form the server reads for it.\n\n    The"
    " server infers each parameter's type from the statement. `PgValue::text` gives the text each variant"
