    "red> value) : Option<String>\u{1f}The text `value` is sent as; `None` for `Null`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgValue::tex"
    "t(ref<PgValue, shared> value) : Option<String>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    The text `value"
    "` is sent as; `None` for `Null`.\n\n    An integer and a float as decimal text (a float that is not fi"
    "nite as `Infinity`, `-Infinity` or `NaN`),\n    a bool as `t` or `f`, bytes as bytea's hex form (`\\x`"
    " and the hex digits).\n\n    Example, \"PgValue::text: what is sent\":\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PgV"
    "alue::text(&Bool(true))) == \"t\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PgValue::text(&Bytes(Vec::filled(2, "
    "0xAB: u8)))) == \"\\\\xabab\");\n        assert(Option::unwrap(PgValue::text(&Float(1.0 / 0.0))) == \"Infi"
    "nity\");\n        assert(Option::is_none(&PgValue::text(&Null)));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgColumn\u{1f}s"
