    "inuously; it has not been independently audited.\n\n    One statement runs at a time, its parameters b"
    "ound (never spliced into the SQL text), and rows come back\n    as text. A connection is one thread's"
    ": a program that queries from several threads keeps a connection\n    per thread. `notices` holds the"
    " notices received so far, for the program to read and clear;\n    `max_result` is the most a statemen"
    "t's rows may take in bytes (16 MiB). Dropping a connection without\n    `PgConnection::close` closes "
    "the socket without telling the server. No binary rows, cursors, COPY,\n    LISTEN/NOTIFY, cancellatio"
    "n or channel binding.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::database::postgres\u{1f}PgConnection::connect\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::con"
    "nect(StringView url) : Result<PgConnection, PgError>\u{1f}Connects to the server `url` names, with a 30-s"
    "econd timeout and the system's trusted roots.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn PgConnection::connect(StringView url) : Res"
    "ult<PgConnection, PgError>\n    in `std::database::postgres`\n\n    Connects to the server `url` names,"
