    "e.\n\n    - `key`: the member's name, its escapes decoded.\n    - `value`: its value.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::"
    "json\u{1f}Json::parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Json::parse(StringView text) : Result<Json, ParseError>\u{1f}The JSON value"
    " `text` holds, with any white space around it.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Json::parse(StringView text) : Result<Json"
    ", ParseError>\n    in `std::encoding::json`\n\n    The JSON value `text` holds, with any white space ar"
    "ound it.\n\n    - `Err(Empty)` when the text holds no value at all.\n    - `Err(Invalid(i))` at the fir"
    "st byte that does not fit, or the length when the text stops short.\n    - `Err(OutOfRange)` for a nu"
    "mber beyond `f64`, or arrays and objects nested deeper than 512.\n\n    In a string, a surrogate pair "
    "written as two `\\u` escapes is joined, and a lone surrogate becomes U+FFFD.\n\n    Example, \"Json::par"
    "se: where the error is\":\n        match (Json::parse(\"[1, 2\"))\n        {\n            Err(Invalid(i)) "
    ": assert(i == 5),\n            _               : assert(false),\n        }\n        match (Json::parse("
    "\"[1] x\"))\n        {\n            Err(Invalid(i)) : assert(i == 4),\n            _               : asse"
    "rt(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::json\u{1f}Json::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Json::text(ref<Json, shared> j) :"
    " String\u{1f}The value `j` as compact JSON text: no white space, members and elements in order.\u{1f}\u{1f}export f"
    "n Json::text(ref<Json, shared> j) : String\n    in `std::encoding::json`\n\n    The value `j` as compac"
    "t JSON text: no white space, members and elements in order.\n\n    A whole number within 2^53 is writt"
    "en without a fraction, any other in the shortest digits that read back\n    as it, and a NaN or an in"
    "finity, which JSON cannot write, as `null`. Strings escape `\"`, `\\` and the\n    control characters; "
    "other characters, non-ASCII included, are written as they are. Apart from a NaN or an\n    infinity, "
    "`Json::parse` of the text gives `j` back.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::json\u{1f}Json::pretty\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Json::pret"
    "ty(ref<Json, shared> j) : String\u{1f}The value `j` as JSON text for people: one element or member per li"
    "ne, two spaces per level.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Json::pretty(ref<Json, shared> j) : String\n    in `std::encodin"
    "g::json`\n\n    The value `j` as JSON text for people: one element or member per line, two spaces per "
    "level.\n\n    A key is followed by `: `, an empty array or object stays `[]` or `{}`, and there is no "
    "newline at the\n    end. Numbers and strings are written as `Json::text` writes them.\n\n    Example, \""
    "Json::pretty: the layout\":\n        Json a = JsonArray(Vec::new());\n        Json::push(&mut a, JsonNu"
    "ll);\n        Json::push(&mut a, JsonText(\"x\"));\n        String p = Json::pretty(&a);\n        assert("
    "p == \"[\\n  null,\\n  \\\"x\\\"\\n]\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::json\u{1f}Json::get\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Json::get(ref<Json, sha"
