    "ion<ref<Json, shared>> from j\n    in `std::encoding::json`\n\n    The value of the first member named "
    "`key` when `j` is an object, else `None`.\n\n    `None` also when there is no such member.\n\n    Exampl"
    "e, \"Json::get: reading a document\":\n        Json doc = Result::unwrap(Json::parse(\"{\\\"name\\\": \\\"ok\\\""
    ", \\\"n\\\": [1, 2.5]}\"));\n        assert(Option::unwrap(Json::as_text(Option::unwrap(Json::get(&doc, \"n"
    "ame\")))) == \"ok\");\n        auto n = Option::unwrap(Json::get(&doc, \"n\"));\n        assert(Json::as_i6"
    "4(Option::unwrap(Json::at(n, 0))) == Some(1: i64));\n        assert(Json::as_i64(Option::unwrap(Json:"
    ":at(n, 1))) == None);\n        assert(Option::is_none(&Json::get(&doc, \"missing\")));\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding:"
    ":json\u{1f}Json::at\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Json::at(ref<Json, shared> j, usize i) : Option<ref<Json, shared>>\u{1f}Eleme"
    "nt `i` of `j` when `j` is an array, else `None`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Json::at(ref<Json, shared> j, usize i) :"
    " Option<ref<Json, shared>>\n    in `std::encoding::json`\n\n    Element `i` of `j` when `j` is an array"
    ", else `None`.\n\n    `None` also when `i` is past the end.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::json\u{1f}Json::lookup\u{1f}fn\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn Json::lookup(ref<Json, shared> j, StringView path) : Option<ref<Json, shared>> from j\u{1f}The valu"
    "e at the dotted `path` below `j`: `Json::lookup(&doc, \"servers.0.host\")`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Json::lookup(re"
    "f<Json, shared> j, StringView path) : Option<ref<Json, shared>> from j\n    in `std::encoding::json`\n"
    "\n    The value at the dotted `path` below `j`: `Json::lookup(&doc, \"servers.0.host\")`.\n\n    Each par"
    "t of the path names a member of an object, or, where the value reached is an array, an element by\n  "
    "  its index written in decimal. `None` when any part is not there. A key that itself contains a dot "
    "is\n    reached with `Json::get`.\n\n    Example, \"Json::lookup: a dotted path\":\n        Json doc = Res"
    "ult::unwrap(Json::parse(\"{\\\"servers\\\": [{\\\"host\\\": \\\"a\\\"}, {\\\"host\\\": \\\"b\\\"}], \\\"n\\\": 1}\"));\n       "
    " assert(Option::unwrap(Json::as_text(Option::unwrap(Json::lookup(&doc, \"servers.1.host\")))) == \"b\");"
    "\n        assert(Json::as_i64(Option::unwrap(Json::lookup(&doc, \"n\"))) == Some(1: i64));\n        asse"
    "rt(Option::is_none(&Json::lookup(&doc, \"servers.2.host\")));\n        assert(Option::is_none(&Json::lo"
