    "sert(i == 1),\n            _               : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml\u{1f}enum"
    "\u{1f}export enum Toml\u{1f}A TOML value: a string, an integer, a float, a boolean, a date-time, an array or a"
    " table.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum Toml\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    A TOML value: a string, an integer, a fl"
    "oat, a boolean, a date-time, an array or a table.\n\n    - `TomlString(s)`: a string, its escapes deco"
    "ded.\n    - `TomlInteger(i)`: an integer, exact in `i64`.\n    - `TomlFloat(x)`: a float, `inf` and `n"
    "an` included.\n    - `TomlBool(b)`: `true` or `false`.\n    - `TomlDateTime(d)`: one of the four date-"
    "time forms (see `TomlDateTime`).\n    - `TomlArray(items)`: the elements, in order; elements may be o"
    "f different kinds.\n    - `TomlTable(members)`: the members in the order read or added; a key occurs "
    "once.\n\n    The variant names carry `Toml` so that none clashes with another `std` enum's. Dropping a"
    " `Toml` frees the\n    whole tree.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}TomlMember\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct TomlMember\u{1f}O"
    "ne member of a TOML table: its key and its value.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct TomlMember\n    in `std::encoding::t"
    "oml`\n\n    One member of a TOML table: its key and its value.\n\n    - `key`: the member's name, one ke"
    "y part (a dotted key `a.b` is a member `a` holding a table with a member `b`).\n    - `value`: its va"
    "lue.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}TomlDateKind\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export enum TomlDateKind\u{1f}Which of the four date-time fo"
    "rms a `TomlDateTime` is.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum TomlDateKind\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    Which of the fo"
    "ur date-time forms a `TomlDateTime` is.\n\n    - `TomlOffsetDateTime`: a date, a time and an offset fr"
    "om UTC: `1979-05-27T07:32:00Z`, `…-08:00`.\n    - `TomlLocalDateTime`: a date and a time with no of"
    "fset: `1979-05-27T07:32:00`.\n    - `TomlLocalDate`: a date alone: `1979-05-27`.\n    - `TomlLocalTime"
    "`: a time alone: `07:32:00`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}TomlDateTime\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct TomlDateTime\u{1f}A "
    "TOML date-time: the fields of RFC 3339's form, and `kind`, which of the four forms it is.\u{1f}\u{1f}export st"
    "ruct TomlDateTime\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    A TOML date-time: the fields of RFC 3339's form,"
    " and `kind`, which of the four forms it is.\n\n    - `kind`: the form; the fields a form does not have"
    " are 0.\n    - `year`, `month`, `day`: the date (`month` 1 to 12, `day` 1 to the month's length).\n   "
    " - `hour`, `minute`, `second`: the time (`second` up to 60 for a leap second).\n    - `nanoseconds`: "
    "the fraction of the second, 0 to 999 999 999; digits beyond nine are dropped when read.\n    - `offse"
    "t_minutes`: the offset from UTC in minutes, `-1439` to `1439`; 0 for every other form.\n\n    A plain "
    "struct, assigned by copying. `TomlDateTime::text` writes it as the format does.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::tom"
    "l\u{1f}Toml::parse\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::parse(StringView text) : Result<Toml, ParseError>\u{1f}The TOML document"
    " `text` holds, as a table.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::parse(StringView text) : Result<Toml, ParseError>\n    in"
    " `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The TOML document `text` holds, as a table.\n\n    The whole of TOML 1.0: "
    "tables and arrays of tables under headers, dotted keys, inline tables, the four\n    string forms wit"
    "h every escape, integers in decimal, hexadecimal, octal and binary with underscores,\n    floats with"
    " `inf` and `nan`, and the four date-time forms. An empty document is an empty table.\n\n    - `Err(Inv"
    "alid(i))` at the first byte that does not fit, or at a key that is defined twice or would\n      add "
    "to a table the format has closed (one defined by an earlier header, or an inline table).\n    - `Err("
    "OutOfRange)` for an integer beyond `i64`, a float beyond `f64`, or arrays and inline tables\n      ne"
    "sted deeper than 512.\n\n    `Err(Empty)` never occurs: a document with no key is an empty table.\n\n   "
    " Example, \"Toml::parse: a configuration file\":\n        Toml doc = Result::unwrap(Toml::parse(\"title "
    "= \\\"Example\\\"\\n[owner]\\nname = \\\"Tom\\\"\\ndob = 1979-05-27T07:32:00-08:00\\n[database]\\nports = [ 8001,"
    " 8001, 8002 ]\\nenabled = true\\ntemp_targets = { cpu = 79.5, case = 72.0 }\\n[[servers]]\\nip = \\\"10.0."
    "0.1\\\"\\n[[servers]]\\nip = \\\"10.0.0.2\\\"\\n\"));\n        assert(Option::unwrap(Toml::as_text(Option::unwr"
    "ap(Toml::lookup(&doc, \"owner.name\")))) == \"Tom\");\n        assert(Toml::as_i64(Option::unwrap(Toml::l"
    "ookup(&doc, \"database.ports.2\"))) == Some(8002: i64));\n        assert(Toml::as_f64(Option::unwrap(To"
    "ml::lookup(&doc, \"database.temp_targets.cpu\"))) == Some(79.5));\n        assert(Option::unwrap(Toml::"
    "as_text(Option::unwrap(Toml::lookup(&doc, \"servers.1.ip\")))) == \"10.0.0.2\");\n        TomlDateTime do"
    "b = Option::unwrap(Toml::as_datetime(Option::unwrap(Toml::lookup(&doc, \"owner.dob\"))));\n        asse"
    "rt(dob.year == 1979 && dob.hour == 7 && dob.offset_minutes == -480);\n\n    Example, \"Toml::parse: whe"
    "re the error is\":\n        match (Toml::parse(\"a = 1\\nb = \\n\"))\n        {\n            Err(Invalid(i))"
    " : assert(i == 10),\n            _               : assert(false),\n        }\n        match (Toml::pars"
    "e(\"a = 1\\na = 2\\n\"))\n        {\n            Err(Invalid(i)) : assert(i == 6),\n            _          "
    "     : assert(false),\n        }\n        match (Toml::parse(\"n = 9223372036854775808\"))\n        {\n   "
    "         Err(OutOfRange) : {},\n            _               : assert(false),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encodin"
    "g::toml\u{1f}TomlDateTime::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn TomlDateTime::text(ref<TomlDateTime, shared> d) : String\u{1f}The"
    " date-time as TOML (and RFC 3339) writes it: the date, `T`, the time, its fraction when there is one"
    ", and the offset as `Z` or `±HH:MM`; a local form leaves out what it does not have.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml"
    "DateTime::text(ref<TomlDateTime, shared> d) : String\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n\n    The date-time"
    " as TOML (and RFC 3339) writes it: the date, `T`, the time, its fraction when there is one,\n    and "
    "the offset as `Z` or `±HH:MM`; a local form leaves out what it does not have.\n\n    Example, \"TomlDa"
    "teTime::text: the four forms\":\n        String text = \"a = 1979-05-27T07:32:00.999999Z\\nb = 1979-05-2"
    "7T00:32:00.5-07:00\\nc = 1979-05-27T07:32:00\\nd = 1979-05-27\\ne = 07:32:00\\n\";\n        Toml doc = Res"
    "ult::unwrap(Toml::parse(&text));\n        assert(Toml::text(&doc) == text);\n        TomlDateTime b = "
    "Option::unwrap(Toml::as_datetime(Option::unwrap(Toml::get(&doc, \"b\"))));\n        assert(b.nanosecond"
    "s == 500000000 && b.offset_minutes == -420 && TomlDateTime::text(&b) == \"1979-05-27T00:32:00.5-07:00"
    "\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::text(ref<Toml, shared> t) : String\u{1f}The value"
    " `t` as TOML text.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::text(ref<Toml, shared> t) : String\n    in `std::encoding::toml`\n"
    "\n    The value `t` as TOML text.\n\n    A table is written as a document: its plain members as `key = "
    "value` lines, then each member that is a\n    table under a `[header]`, and each non-empty array of t"
    "ables under `[[headers]]`, in order, recursively; a\n    key is bare when it can be and quoted otherw"
    "ise. Strings are basic strings with `\"`, `\\` and the control\n    characters escaped; a float is writ"
    "ten in the shortest digits that read back as it, with `inf` and `nan`;\n    a date-time as `TomlDateT"
    "ime::text` writes it. A value that is not a table is written in the form it takes\n    after `=`: arr"
    "ays as `[a, b]`, inline tables as `{ k = v }`. Comments are not kept. `Toml::parse` of the text\n    "
    "gives `t` back, the plain members of each table before its sub-tables.\n\n    Example, \"Toml::text: th"
    "e layout\":\n        Toml doc = Result::unwrap(Toml::parse(\"[server]\\nhost = \\\"example.org\\\"\\nports = "
    "[80, 443]\\n[server.tls]\\ncert = 'a b'\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"ann\\\"\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"bob\\\"\\n\"));\n  "
    "      String t = Toml::text(&doc);\n        assert(t == \"[server]\\nhost = \\\"example.org\\\"\\nports = [8"
    "0, 443]\\n\\n[server.tls]\\ncert = \\\"a b\\\"\\n\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"ann\\\"\\n\\n[[users]]\\nname = \\\"bob\\\"\\n\""
    ");\n        assert(Toml::text(&Result::unwrap(Toml::parse(&t))) == t);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::encoding::toml\u{1f}Toml::ge"
    "t\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn Toml::get(ref<Toml, shared> t, StringView key) : Option<ref<Toml, shared>> from t\u{1f}The"
    " value of the member named `key` when `t` is a table, else `None`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn Toml::get(ref<Toml, sh"
