    "l::set(&mut doc, \"name\", TomlString(\"demo 2\"));\n        assert(Toml::text(&doc) == \"name = \\\"demo 2\\"
    "\"\\n\\n[server]\\nports = [8080, 8081]\\ndebug = false\\n\");\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}CompressError\u{1f}enum\u{1f}export en"
    "um CompressError\u{1f}Why a stream could not be decompressed.\u{1f}\u{1f}export enum CompressError\n    in `std::com"
    "press`\n\n    Why a stream could not be decompressed.\n\n    - `Corrupt(i)`: the stream is not DEFLATE ("
    "or not the wrapper asked for), or its checksum does not match,\n      first seen at byte `i`.\n    - `"
    "Truncated`: the stream ends before its last block or its trailer.\n    - `Oversize`: the output would"
    " exceed the `max` given.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}CompressError::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CompressError::text(ref<Co"
    "mpressError, shared> e) : str\u{1f}A short description of `e` for a message, such as `corrupt compressed "
    "data`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CompressError::text(ref<CompressError, shared> e) : str\n    in `std::compress`\n\n  "
    "  A short description of `e` for a message, such as `corrupt compressed data`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}infla"
    "te\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn inflate(slice<u8, shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\u{1f}The byte"
    "s a raw DEFLATE stream (RFC 1951, no header or checksum) encodes, at most `max` of them.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn "
    "inflate(slice<u8, shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\n    in `std::compress`\n\n"
    "    The bytes a raw DEFLATE stream (RFC 1951, no header or checksum) encodes, at most `max` of them."
    "\n\n    `Err(Oversize)` as soon as the output would exceed `max`: a limit against a small stream that "
    "expands\n    without bound. `Err(Truncated)` when `data` ends inside a block; `Err(Corrupt(i))` at by"
    "te `i` for a\n    malformed block. Bytes after the final block are ignored. Reads stored, fixed and d"
    "ynamic Huffman blocks.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}deflate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn deflate(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8"
    ">\u{1f}`data` compressed as a raw DEFLATE stream (RFC 1951, no header or checksum).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn deflate(sl"
    "ice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    `data` compressed as a raw DEFLATE strea"
    "m (RFC 1951, no header or checksum).\n\n    One fixed strategy, so every implementation writes the sam"
    "e bytes: LZ77 over a 32 KiB window, each block\n    stored, fixed or dynamic Huffman, whichever is sh"
    "ortest. Empty data is one empty block (`03 00`).\n\n    Example, \"deflate: empty data, and adler32\":\n "
    "       Vec<u8> nothing = Vec::new();\n        Vec<u8> empty = deflate(&nothing);\n        assert(Vec::"
    "len(&empty) == 2 && empty[0] == 0x03 && empty[1] == 0x00);\n        assert(Vec::len(&Result::unwrap(i"
    "nflate(&empty, 0))) == 0);\n        assert(adler32(b\"Wikipedia\") == 300286872);\n        assert(adler3"
    "2(&nothing) == 1);\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}adler32\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn adler32(slice<u8, shared> data) : u32\u{1f}The Ad"
    "ler-32 checksum of `data` (RFC 1950), zlib's checksum; 1 for no bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn adler32(slice<u8, "
    "shared> data) : u32\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    The Adler-32 checksum of `data` (RFC 1950), zlib's c"
    "hecksum; 1 for no bytes.\n\n    For CRC-32, gzip's checksum, use `crc32` in `std::crypto`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::comp"
    "ress\u{1f}zlib_deflate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn zlib_deflate(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}`data` compressed as a"
    " zlib stream (RFC 1950): a two-byte header, the DEFLATE stream, the Adler-32.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn zlib_deflat"
    "e(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    `data` compressed as a zlib stream ("
    "RFC 1950): a two-byte header, the DEFLATE stream, the Adler-32.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}zlib_inflate\u{1f}fn\u{1f}expo"
    "rt fn zlib_inflate(slice<u8, shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\u{1f}The bytes a z"
    "lib stream encodes, at most `max` of them, its header checked and its checksum verified.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn "
    "zlib_inflate(slice<u8, shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\n    in `std::compre"
    "ss`\n\n    The bytes a zlib stream encodes, at most `max` of them, its header checked and its checksum"
    " verified.\n\n    `Err(Corrupt(0))` for a header that is not DEFLATE without a preset dictionary; `Err"
    "(Corrupt(i))` at the\n    trailer when the Adler-32 does not match; `Err(Truncated)` for fewer than 6"
    " bytes or a missing trailer;\n    otherwise as `inflate`, `Err(Oversize)` included.\n\n    Example, \"zl"
    "ib_inflate: a wrong checksum\":\n        Vec<u8> z = zlib_deflate(b\"hello hello hello\");\n        usize"
    " last = Vec::len(&z) - 1;\n        z[last] = z[last] ^ 1;\n        match (zlib_inflate(&z, 100))\n     "
    "   {\n            Err(Corrupt(at)) : assert(at == last - 3),\n            _                : assert(fa"
    "lse),\n        }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}gzip\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn gzip(slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\u{1f}`data` comp"
    "ressed as a gzip file (RFC 1952), with no name, time or extra fields in its header.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn gzip("
    "slice<u8, shared> data) : Vec<u8>\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    `data` compressed as a gzip file (RFC "
    "1952), with no name, time or extra fields in its header.\n\n    The trailer holds the CRC-32 and the l"
    "ength of `data` modulo 2 to the power 32.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::compress\u{1f}gunzip\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn gunzip(slice<u8, share"
    "d> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, CompressError>\u{1f}The bytes a gzip file encodes, every member in "
    "turn, at most `max` of them.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn gunzip(slice<u8, shared> data, usize max) : Result<Vec<u8>, "
    "CompressError>\n    in `std::compress`\n\n    The bytes a gzip file encodes, every member in turn, at m"
    "ost `max` of them.\n\n    Each header's optional fields are skipped. `Err(Corrupt(i))` at a header tha"
    "t is not gzip's, or at a\n    trailer whose CRC-32 or length does not match; `Err(Truncated)` for a m"
    "ember cut short; otherwise as\n    `inflate`, `Err(Oversize)` included.\n\n    Example, \"gunzip: round "
    "trip and the size limit\":\n        Vec<u8> data = Vec::filled(1000, b'a');\n        Vec<u8> packed = g"
    "zip(&data);\n        assert(Vec::len(&packed) < 100);\n        Vec<u8> back = Result::unwrap(gunzip(&p"
    "acked, 1000));\n        assert(Vec::len(&back) == 1000 && back[999] == b'a');\n        match (gunzip(&"
    "packed, 999))\n        {\n            Err(Oversize) : {},\n            _             : assert(false),\n "
    "       }\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}NulError\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct NulError\u{1f}The error of text that holds a NUL byte, "
    "which C would take as its end.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct NulError\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    The error of text that"
    " holds a NUL byte, which C would take as its end.\n\n    `offset` is the position of the first NUL.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}"
    "std::ffi\u{1f}NulError::text\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn NulError::text(ref<NulError, shared> e) : str\u{1f}A short descripti"
    "on of the error for messages: `\"holds a NUL byte\"`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn NulError::text(ref<NulError, shared> "
    "e) : str\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    A short description of the error for messages: `\"holds a NUL byte\"`."
    "\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString\u{1f}struct\u{1f}export struct CString\u{1f}Text followed by one NUL byte, for a C function tha"
    "t takes `const char *`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export struct CString\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    Text followed by one NUL byte,"
    " for a C function that takes `const char *`.\n\n    Made by `CString::new` or `CString::from_bytes`, w"
    "hich refuse text that already holds a NUL. `CString::ptr` is\n    the address to pass; it stays valid"
    " while the `CString` lives, even if the `CString` itself is moved, and\n    dropping the `CString` fr"
    "ees the bytes. The C function must not write through the address or keep it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString::fro"
    "m_bytes\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CString::from_bytes(slice<u8, shared> b) : Result<CString, NulError>\u{1f}`b` with a"
    " NUL byte after it, or `Err` with the position of the first NUL already in `b`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::"
    "from_bytes(slice<u8, shared> b) : Result<CString, NulError>\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    `b` with a NUL by"
    "te after it, or `Err` with the position of the first NUL already in `b`.\n\n    The bytes need not be "
    "UTF-8: a path or a name from another system is often not.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString::new\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CStri"
    "ng::new(StringView s) : Result<CString, NulError>\u{1f}`s` with a NUL byte after it, or `Err` with the po"
    "sition of the first NUL already in `s`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::new(StringView s) : Result<CString, NulE"
    "rror>\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    `s` with a NUL byte after it, or `Err` with the position of the first N"
    "UL already in `s`.\n\n    A literal where a `StringView` is expected is made into one: `CString::new(\""
    "HOME\")`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString::ptr\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CString::ptr(ref<CString, shared> c) : rawptr<u8>\u{1f}The "
    "address of the first byte, to pass to C as a `const char *`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::ptr(ref<CString, sh"
    "ared> c) : rawptr<u8>\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    The address of the first byte, to pass to C as a `const"
    " char *`.\n\n    Taking the address is safe; the call that uses it is inside `unsafe`. The address is "
    "valid until the\n    `CString` is dropped.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CString::len\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CString::len(ref<CStr"
    "ing, shared> c) : usize\u{1f}The length of the text, without the NUL.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::len(ref<CString"
    ", shared> c) : usize\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    The length of the text, without the NUL.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}CStr"
    "ing::as_bytes\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn CString::as_bytes(ref<CString, shared> c) : slice<u8, shared>\u{1f}The text wi"
    "thout the NUL, as bytes.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn CString::as_bytes(ref<CString, shared> c) : slice<u8, shared>\n  "
    "  in `std::ffi`\n\n    The text without the NUL, as bytes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}copy_to_raw\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn copy_to"
    "_raw<T: plain>(slice<T, shared> s, rawptr<T> p)\u{1f}The elements of `s`, plain data, copied to C memory "
    "at `p`: an output buffer a C caller owns (D-0257).\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn copy_to_raw<T: plain>(slice<T, shared>"
    " s, rawptr<T> p)\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    The elements of `s`, plain data, copied to C memory at `p`: "
    "an output\n    buffer a C caller owns (D-0257). Called inside `unsafe { }`\n    (`[Trusted-Call]`): th"
    "e caller vouches that `p` has room for them and\n    that nothing else uses that memory for the call."
    "\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::ffi\u{1f}is_null\u{1f}fn\u{1f}export fn is_null<T>(rawptr<T> p) : bool\u{1f}Whether `p` is C's `NULL`, the addre"
    "ss `null_rawptr<T>()`.\u{1f}\u{1f}export fn is_null<T>(rawptr<T> p) : bool\n    in `std::ffi`\n\n    Whether `p` "
    "is C's `NULL`, the address `null_rawptr<T>()`.\n\n    C functions return `NULL` for \"none\": `getenv` o"
    "f a name that is not set, `fopen` of a file that cannot be\n    opened. Testing for it is safe; readi"
    "ng through `p` is not.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::core\u{1f}Result::map_err\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn Result::map_err<T, E1, E2>(Result<"
    "T, E1> r, fn(E1) : E2 f) : Result<T, E2>\u{1f}Keeps an `Ok` as it is and maps an `Err` through `f`: `matc"
    "h (r) { Ok(v) : Ok(v), Err(e) : Err(f(e)) }`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn Result::map_err<T, E1, E2>(Result<T, E1> r, fn(E1)"
    " : E2 f) : Result<T, E2>\n    in `std::core`\n\n    Keeps an `Ok` as it is and maps an `Err` through `f"
    "`: `match (r) { Ok(v) : Ok(v), Err(e) : Err(f(e)) }`.\n    It is the step that turns a library's erro"
    "r into a program's own before `?` passes it on. `r` is\n    consumed; `f` runs only for an `Err`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}s"
    "td::io\u{1f}printf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn printf(str f, a1, …, an)\u{1f}Writes the arguments to standard output as t"
    "he format `f` says (`spec/21` §2f, `rule.stdlib.format`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn printf(str f, a1, …, an)\n    in `st"
    "d::io`\n\n    Writes the arguments to standard output as the format `f` says (`spec/21` §2f, `rule.st"
    "dlib.format`).\n    `f` is a string literal, so the format and the arguments are checked when the pro"
    "gram is compiled and\n    nothing about it can fail at run time. The conversions are C's: `%d` for an"
    "y integer type (there is no\n    `%ld`), `%u`, `%x`, `%X`, `%o`, `%b` (binary) for an integer's bits "
    "in its own width, `%f`, `%e`, `%g` for\n    `f32` and `f64`, `%s` for a `str`, a `ref<String, shared>"
    "` or a `bool`, and `%v` for any printable value\n    or enum \"as CobaltC writes it\" (an enum's varian"
    "t name; a float that reads back as the same value). Width\n    and precision may be `*`, taking the n"
    "ext argument (a `usize`). A reference to a number, a `bool` or a\n    `str` prints as what it refers "
    "to, so `foreach (x in &v) { printf(\"%d\\n\", x); }` prints the elements.\n    Output is buffered (D-017"
    "8) and written out when the buffer fills, at `flush_stdout()`, and when the\n    program ends.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std:"
    ":io\u{1f}eprintf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn eprintf(str f, a1, …, an)\u{1f}Writes the arguments to standard error as the"
    " format `f` says, with `printf`'s conversions.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn eprintf(str f, a1, …, an)\n    in `std::io`\n\n   "
    " Writes the arguments to standard error as the format `f` says, with `printf`'s conversions. For\n   "
    " messages that are not the program's output: errors, warnings, progress. Standard error is written a"
    "t\n    once, with nothing held back, so its text and standard output's interleave in the order the ca"
    "lls ran\n    (after a `flush_stdout()`, exactly).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}sprintf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn sprintf(str f, a"
    "1, …, an) : String\u{1f}The text `printf` would write for the same arguments, as a new `String` instead"
    " of output.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn sprintf(str f, a1, …, an) : String\n    in `std::text`\n\n    The text `printf` would"
    " write for the same arguments, as a new `String` instead of output. The format is\n    checked when t"
    "he program is compiled, as `printf`'s is.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::text\u{1f}String::appendf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn String::appendf"
    "(ref<String, exclusive> s, str f, a1, …, an)\u{1f}Appends to `*s` the text `printf` would write for the"
    " same arguments; `String::append` of `sprintf`'s result, without the intermediate `String`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn Stri"
    "ng::appendf(ref<String, exclusive> s, str f, a1, …, an)\n    in `std::text`\n\n    Appends to `*s` th"
    "e text `printf` would write for the same arguments; `String::append` of `sprintf`'s\n    result, with"
    "out the intermediate `String`. The common way to build a line piece by piece before printing\n    or "
    "keeping it once.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::io\u{1f}File::printf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn File::printf(ref<File, exclusive> f, str form"
    "at, a1, …, an) : Result<void, FileError>\u{1f}Writes the formatted text to the open file `*f`, as `prin"
    "tf` would to standard output (D-0059); the format is checked when the program is compiled.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn File:"
    ":printf(ref<File, exclusive> f, str format, a1, …, an) : Result<void, FileError>\n    in `std::io`\n"
    "\n    Writes the formatted text to the open file `*f`, as `printf` would to standard output (D-0059);"
    " the\n    format is checked when the program is compiled. A write that fails is the `Err`, as for `Fi"
    "le::write`.\n    `File` itself is `std::fs`'s type; this function is registered with the `printf` fam"
    "ily in `std::io`,\n    and `import std;` brings in both.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::net\u{1f}TcpStream::printf\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn "
    "TcpStream::printf(ref<TcpStream, exclusive> s, str format, a1, …, an) : Result<void, NetError>\u{1f}Wri"
    "tes the formatted text to the connected stream `*s`, as `File::printf` does to a file; the whole tex"
    "t is written or the `Err` says why (`[Stream-Write]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn TcpStream::printf(ref<TcpStream, exclusiv"
    "e> s, str format, a1, …, an) : Result<void, NetError>\n    in `std::net`\n\n    Writes the formatted "
    "text to the connected stream `*s`, as `File::printf` does to a file; the whole text\n    is written o"
    "r the `Err` says why (`[Stream-Write]`). A line protocol's reply in one call:\n    `TcpStream::printf"
    "(&mut c, \"%d %s\\r\\n\", code, text)?`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::core\u{1f}assert\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn assert(bool c), fn assert(boo"
    "l c, str f, a1, …, an)\u{1f}Checks `c` and, if it is false, faults with `diag.assert-failed`, reporting"
    " the formatted message if one is given (`spec/18` §1a, `rule.fail.assert`, D-0065).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn assert(bool"
    " c), fn assert(bool c, str f, a1, …, an)\n    in `std::core`\n\n    Checks `c` and, if it is false, f"
    "aults with `diag.assert-failed`, reporting the formatted message if one\n    is given (`spec/18` §1a"
    ", `rule.fail.assert`, D-0065). The message's arguments are evaluated only when the\n    assertion fai"
    "ls. An assertion is part of the program's meaning: there is no build in which it is left\n    out, an"
    "d `--check` sees its format as it sees `printf`'s. The fault unwinds like any other, so\n    destruct"
    "ors run and a supervised task reports it to its parent.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::process\u{1f}exit\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn exit(u8 s"
    "tatus) : never\u{1f}Ends the program with exit status `status` (`[Exit]`, `spec/21` §2k, D-0150).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn ex"
    "it(u8 status) : never\n    in `std::process`\n\n    Ends the program with exit status `status` (`[Exit]"
    "`, `spec/21` §2k, D-0150). The calling thread unwinds\n    first, so its destructors run and standar"
    "d output is written out; other threads are not waited for. The\n    result type is `never`, so a bran"
    "ch that calls `exit` needs no value of its own. `fn main() : u8`'s return\n    value is the ordinary "
    "way to set the status; `exit` is for deep inside a program.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}sqrt\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn sqrt(T x"
    ") : T\u{1f}The square root of `x`, correctly rounded (`[Float-Fn]`, `spec/21` §3d, D-0091): every confor"
    "ming implementation gives the same bits.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn sqrt(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The square root o"
    "f `x`, correctly rounded (`[Float-Fn]`, `spec/21` §3d, D-0091): every conforming\n    implementation"
    " gives the same bits. A NaN for a negative `x`; `-0.0` for `-0.0`; a NaN in gives a NaN out.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::"
    "math\u{1f}floor\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn floor(T x) : T\u{1f}`x` rounded to an integral value toward negative infinity, "
    "exactly (`[Float-Fn]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn floor(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to an integral value "
    "toward negative infinity, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`). A NaN or an infinity is\n    returned as it is.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}s"
    "td::math\u{1f}ceil\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn ceil(T x) : T\u{1f}`x` rounded to an integral value toward positive infinity"
    ", exactly (`[Float-Fn]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn ceil(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to an integral value"
    " toward positive infinity, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}round\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn round(T x) : T\u{1f}`"
    "x` rounded to the nearest integral value, halfway cases away from zero (`2.5` to `3.0`, `-2.5` to `-"
    "3.0`), exactly (`[Float-Fn]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn round(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to the nearest"
    " integral value, halfway cases away from zero (`2.5` to `3.0`, `-2.5` to\n    `-3.0`), exactly (`[Flo"
    "at-Fn]`). Convert the result with `rule.arith.convert` when an integer is wanted.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}trunc\u{1f}"
    "built in fn\u{1f}fn trunc(T x) : T\u{1f}`x` rounded to an integral value toward zero, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`): "
    "the fractional part dropped.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn trunc(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` rounded to an integral v"
    "alue toward zero, exactly (`[Float-Fn]`): the fractional part dropped.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}ln\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn"
    " ln(T x) : T\u{1f}The natural logarithm of `x`, within one unit in the last place of the mathematical val"
    "ue (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0101): the platform's C library computes it, so the result is the sa"
    "me on one platform and may differ in the last bit between platforms.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn ln(T x) : T\n    in `std::ma"
    "th`\n\n    The natural logarithm of `x`, within one unit in the last place of the mathematical value\n "
    "   (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0101): the platform's C library computes it, so the result is the sa"
    "me on one\n    platform and may differ in the last bit between platforms. A NaN for a negative `x`; n"
    "egative infinity for\n    `±0`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}exp\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn exp(T x) : T\u{1f}`e` to the power `x`, wi"
    "thin one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn exp(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n   "
    " `e` to the power `x`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`). Overflows to in"
    "finity\n    as IEEE-754 says.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}log2\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn log2(T x) : T\u{1f}The base-2 logarithm of `"
    "x`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`); a NaN for a negative `x`, negative"
    " infinity for `±0`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn log2(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The base-2 logarithm of `x`, within o"
    "ne unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`); a NaN for a\n    negative `x`, negative infinit"
    "y for `±0`. For an integer's bit length, `integer` arithmetic is exact and\n    cheaper.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math"
    "\u{1f}log10\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn log10(T x) : T\u{1f}The base-10 logarithm of `x`, within one unit in the last place"
    " (`[Float-Transcendental]`); a NaN for a negative `x`, negative infinity for `±0`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn log10(T x) :"
    " T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The base-10 logarithm of `x`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-"
    "Transcendental]`); a NaN for a\n    negative `x`, negative infinity for `±0`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}sin\u{1f}built "
    "in fn\u{1f}fn sin(T x) : T\u{1f}The sine of `x`, an angle in radians, within one unit in the last place (`[Flo"
    "at-Transcendental]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn sin(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The sine of `x`, an angle in radians,"
    " within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}cos\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn cos(T "
    "x) : T\u{1f}The cosine of `x`, an angle in radians, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcende"
    "ntal]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn cos(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The cosine of `x`, an angle in radians, within one"
    " unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}tan\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn tan(T x) : T\u{1f}The "
    "tangent of `x`, an angle in radians, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`).\u{1f}\u{1f}"
    "fn tan(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The tangent of `x`, an angle in radians, within one unit in "
