    "e of `x`, in radians in `[-π/2, π/2]`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`"
    ", D-0181); a NaN for `x` outside `[-1, 1]`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn asin(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The arc sine o"
    "f `x`, in radians in `[-π/2, π/2]`, within one unit in the last place\n    (`[Float-Transcendental]"
    "`, D-0181); a NaN for `x` outside `[-1, 1]`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}acos\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn acos(T x) : T\u{1f}The arc c"
    "osine of `x`, in radians in `[0, π]`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`, "
    "D-0181); a NaN for `x` outside `[-1, 1]`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn acos(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The arc cosine o"
    "f `x`, in radians in `[0, π]`, within one unit in the last place\n    (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0"
    "181); a NaN for `x` outside `[-1, 1]`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}atan\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn atan(T x) : T\u{1f}The arc tangent"
    " of `x`, in radians in `(-π/2, π/2)`, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental]`,"
    " D-0181).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn atan(T x) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    The arc tangent of `x`, in radians in `(-π/2, π"
    "/2)`, within one unit in the last place\n    (`[Float-Transcendental]`, D-0181). For an angle from tw"
    "o coordinates use `atan2`, which knows the quadrant.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}std::math\u{1f}atan2\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn atan2(T y, T x"
    ") : T\u{1f}The angle of the point `(x, y)` from the positive x axis, in radians in `(-π, π]`, within on"
    "e unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental-2]`); C's `atan2`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn atan2(T y, T x) : T\n    in `"
