    "-point operands, within one unit in the last place (`[Float-Transcendental-2]`); C's `pow`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn powf"
    "(T x, T y) : T\n    in `std::math`\n\n    `x` to the power `y` for floating-point operands, within one "
    "unit in the last place\n    (`[Float-Transcendental-2]`); C's `pow`. For an integer exponent, `pow` ("
    "an ordinary `std::math` function)\n    is exact and checked for overflow.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}drop\u{1f}built i"
    "n fn\u{1f}fn drop<T>(T x)\u{1f}Destroys `x` now, before the end of its scope (`rule.resauth.destroy`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn dro"
    "p<T>(T x)\n    in `the language`\n\n    Destroys `x` now, before the end of its scope (`rule.resauth.de"
    "stroy`). The argument is a place, so `drop(v)`\n    ends the binding `v`; a temporary is destroyed di"
    "rectly. A resource's destructor runs, its memory is freed,\n    and any later use of the binding is `"
    "diag.stale-binding`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}clone\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn clone<T: clone>(ref<T, shared> x) : T\u{1f}A cop"
    "y of the value `x` refers to, made by its type's `clone` (D-0116).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn clone<T: clone>(ref<T, shared"
    "> x) : T\n    in `the language`\n\n    A copy of the value `x` refers to, made by its type's `clone` (D"
    "-0116). A struct or enum whose fields all\n    clone has one derived; a `String`, `Vec` or `Box` copi"
    "es what it owns.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}sizeof\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn sizeof<T>() : usize\u{1f}The size of a value of typ"
    "e `T` in bytes, as the implementation lays it out (`rule.arith.sizeof`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn sizeof<T>() : usize\n   "
    " in `the language`\n\n    The size of a value of type `T` in bytes, as the implementation lays it out "
    "(`rule.arith.sizeof`). Known\n    when the program is compiled, so it may stand in a constant.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the "
    "language\u{1f}alignof\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn alignof<T>() : usize\u{1f}The alignment of type `T` in bytes (`rule.arith"
    ".sizeof`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn alignof<T>() : usize\n    in `the language`\n\n    The alignment of type `T` in bytes (`"
    "rule.arith.sizeof`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}min_value\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn min_value<T>() : T\u{1f}The least value of `"
    "T`, an integer type, `f32` or `f64` (`rule.arith.limits`): `min_value<i32>()` is -2147483648.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn mi"
    "n_value<T>() : T\n    in `the language`\n\n    The least value of `T`, an integer type, `f32` or `f64` "
    "(`rule.arith.limits`): `min_value<i32>()` is\n    -2147483648. For a float it is the most negative fi"
    "nite value.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}max_value\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn max_value<T>() : T\u{1f}The greatest value of `T`, an"
    " integer type, `f32` or `f64` (`rule.arith.limits`): `max_value<u8>()` is 255.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn max_value<T>() : "
    "T\n    in `the language`\n\n    The greatest value of `T`, an integer type, `f32` or `f64` (`rule.arith"
    ".limits`): `max_value<u8>()` is 255.\n    For a float it is the greatest finite value.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language"
    "\u{1f}widen\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn widen<U>(T x) : U\u{1f}`x` as a value of the wider type `U`, which never fails (`ru"
    "le.arith.convert`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn widen<U>(T x) : U\n    in `the language`\n\n    `x` as a value of the wider typ"
    "e `U`, which never fails (`rule.arith.convert`). It is accepted only where\n    `U` holds every value"
    " of `T`: `u8` to `u32` or `i16`, `i32` to `i64`, `f32` to `f64`. The other way is\n    `narrow`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}th"
    "e language\u{1f}narrow\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn narrow<U>(T x) : U\u{1f}`x` as a value of the integer type `U`, checked:"
    " a value `U` cannot hold faults with `diag.arith-overflow` (`rule.arith.convert`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn narrow<U>(T x"
    ") : U\n    in `the language`\n\n    `x` as a value of the integer type `U`, checked: a value `U` cannot"
    " hold faults with\n    `diag.arith-overflow` (`rule.arith.convert`). `checked_narrow` gives an `Optio"
    "n` instead, and\n    `narrow_wrapping` keeps the low bits.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}narrow_wrapping\u{1f}built in fn"
    "\u{1f}fn narrow_wrapping<U>(T x) : U\u{1f}`x` as a value of the integer type `U`, keeping its low bits, as C's"
    " cast does (`rule.arith.convert`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn narrow_wrapping<U>(T x) : U\n    in `the language`\n\n    `x` as"
    " a value of the integer type `U`, keeping its low bits, as C's cast does (`rule.arith.convert`).\n   "
    " Never fails.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}checked_narrow\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn checked_narrow<U>(T x) : Option<U>\u{1f}`Some("
    "x)` as a value of the integer type `U` when `U` holds it, else `None` (`[Checked-Narrow]`, D-0122).\u{1f}"
    "\u{1f}fn checked_narrow<U>(T x) : Option<U>\n    in `the language`\n\n    `Some(x)` as a value of the intege"
    "r type `U` when `U` holds it, else `None` (`[Checked-Narrow]`, D-0122).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}reinterpret\u{1f}b"
    "uilt in fn\u{1f}fn reinterpret<U>(T x) : U\u{1f}The bits of `x` read as a value of `U`, a type of the same siz"
    "e: an integer's bits as the other signedness (`u32` to `i32`), a float's bits as an integer or back "
    "(`rule.arith.convert`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn reinterpret<U>(T x) : U\n    in `the language`\n\n    The bits of `x` read "
    "as a value of `U`, a type of the same size: an integer's bits as the other signedness\n    (`u32` to "
    "`i32`), a float's bits as an integer or back (`rule.arith.convert`). Never fails.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}to_"
    "float\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn to_float<U>(T x) : U\u{1f}The integer `x` as the float type `U` (`f32` or `f64`), ro"
    "unded to the nearest representable value (`rule.arith.convert`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn to_float<U>(T x) : U\n    in `th"
    "e language`\n\n    The integer `x` as the float type `U` (`f32` or `f64`), rounded to the nearest repr"
    "esentable value\n    (`rule.arith.convert`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}to_int\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn to_int<U>(T x) : U\u{1f}"
    "The float `x` as the integer type `U`, its fraction dropped (toward zero), checked: a NaN, an infini"
    "ty or a value `U` cannot hold faults with `diag.arith-overflow` (`rule.arith.convert`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn to_int<U"
    ">(T x) : U\n    in `the language`\n\n    The float `x` as the integer type `U`, its fraction dropped (t"
    "oward zero), checked: a NaN, an infinity or a\n    value `U` cannot hold faults with `diag.arith-over"
    "flow` (`rule.arith.convert`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}wrapping_add\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn wrapping_add<T>(T a, T b) :"
    " T\u{1f}`a + b` kept to the width of `T`, wrapping around instead of faulting (`rule.arith.alt`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn wra"
    "pping_add<T>(T a, T b) : T\n    in `the language`\n\n    `a + b` kept to the width of `T`, wrapping aro"
    "und instead of faulting (`rule.arith.alt`). Also lane by lane\n    on two `simd` values of integer la"
    "nes.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}wrapping_sub\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn wrapping_sub<T>(T a, T b) : T\u{1f}`a - b` kept to the wi"
    "dth of `T`, wrapping around instead of faulting (`rule.arith.alt`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn wrapping_sub<T>(T a, T b) : "
