    "kept to the width of `T`, wrapping around instead of faulting (`rule.arith.alt`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn wrapping_mul<T"
    ">(T a, T b) : T\n    in `the language`\n\n    `a * b` kept to the width of `T`, wrapping around instead"
    " of faulting (`rule.arith.alt`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}saturating_add\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn saturating_add<T>(T a,"
    " T b) : T\u{1f}`a + b`, or the nearest of `min_value<T>()` and `max_value<T>()` when it does not fit (`ru"
    "le.arith.alt`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn saturating_add<T>(T a, T b) : T\n    in `the language`\n\n    `a + b`, or the neare"
    "st of `min_value<T>()` and `max_value<T>()` when it does not fit (`rule.arith.alt`).\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}"
    "saturating_sub\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn saturating_sub<T>(T a, T b) : T\u{1f}`a - b`, or the nearest limit of `T` w"
    "hen it does not fit (`rule.arith.alt`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn saturating_sub<T>(T a, T b) : T\n    in `the language`\n\n "
