    " until no other thread holds `m`, then holds it: the guard reads and writes the value (`g.f`, `*g`)\n"
    "    and lets the mutex go when it is destroyed, at the end of its scope (`rule.conc.lock`). A thread"
    " that\n    faults while holding it poisons it.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}spawn\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn spawn(fn(T1, …, "
    "Tn) : R f, T1 a1, …, Tn an) : handle<R>\u{1f}Runs `f(a1, …, an)` on a new thread and returns at once "
    "with its handle (`rule.conc.spawn`).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn spawn(fn(T1, …, Tn) : R f, T1 a1, …, Tn an) : handle<R>"
    "\n    in `the language`\n\n    Runs `f(a1, …, an)` on a new thread and returns at once with its handl"
    "e (`rule.conc.spawn`). The arguments\n    are moved to the thread or lent to it until `join`; `f` is "
    "a function or a `move` closure. `join(h)` waits\n    for the result.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}join\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}"
    "fn join<T>(handle<T> h) : T\u{1f}Waits for the thread `h` to end and gives its result; a fault in the thr"
    "ead is raised again here (`rule.conc.join`, D-0204).\u{1f}\u{1f}fn join<T>(handle<T> h) : T\n    in `the langua"
    "ge`\n\n    Waits for the thread `h` to end and gives its result; a fault in the thread is raised again"
    " here\n    (`rule.conc.join`, D-0204). `try_join` gives the fault as a value instead.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}"
    "cancel\u{1f}built in fn\u{1f}fn cancel<T>(ref<handle<T>, shared> h)\u{1f}Asks the thread `h` to stop at its next wa"
    "it (`rule.conc.cancel`, D-0204); `join` then raises `diag.thread-cancelled`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn cancel<T>(ref<handl"
    "e<T>, shared> h)\n    in `the language`\n\n    Asks the thread `h` to stop at its next wait (`rule.conc"
    ".cancel`, D-0204); `join` then raises\n    `diag.thread-cancelled`.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}the language\u{1f}join_status\u{1f}built "
    "in fn\u{1f}fn join_status<T>(ref<handle<T>, shared> h, u8 mode) : u64\u{1f}The thread's state, the primitive u"
    "nder `try_join` and `is_finished` (D-0204): 0 while it runs, 1 when it ended with a result, `k + 2` "
    "when it failed with failure `k`.\u{1f}\u{1f}fn join_status<T>(ref<handle<T>, shared> h, u8 mode) : u64\n    in "
    "`the language`\n\n    The thread's state, the primitive under `try_join` and `is_finished` (D-0204): 0"
    " while it runs, 1 when it\n    ended with a result, `k + 2` when it failed with failure `k`. Mode 0 f"
    "irst waits for the end, mode 1 only\n    looks.\n\u{1f}\u{1e}";
